{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread","id":1501114,"title":"Ask a Simple Question, Get A Simple Answer (CoD General) [new thread]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-01-22T23:23:29-08:00","id":1501114,"title":"Ask a Simple Question, Get A Simple Answer (CoD General) [new thread]","content":"So the previous version of the &quot;Ask a simple question...&quot; thread have been closed, and it's been indicated that new threads should be started. I'll kick it off here for a thread for all your miscellaneous Questions!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-23T13:47:38-08:00","id":1501167,"title":"","content":"For a non combat character with minimal stats, skills, and funding, would pepper spray or a stun gun be more mechanically more appropriate for self defense? Does pepper spray/stun guns even work on supernatural stuff like manifested Ephemeral Entities? <br /> <br /> Secondly, I seem to recall archery being able to use Dexterity + Athletics as a dice pool, but I can\u2019t seem to find that in my books. Did my brain just make that up?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-23T17:27:49-08:00","id":1501186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1501167#post1501167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For a non combat character with minimal stats, skills, and funding, would pepper spray or a stun gun be more mechanically more appropriate for self defense? Does pepper spray/stun guns even work on supernatural stuff like manifested Ephemeral Entities?<br /> <br /> Secondly, I seem to recall archery being able to use Dexterity + Athletics as a dice pool, but I can\u2019t seem to find that in my books. Did my brain just make that up?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends. There's like 3 or 4 different builds for Pepper Spray scattered among the rules, and they all use different mechanics.<br /> <br /> As for bows, Hurt Locker allows you to use either, and there's a Style Merit for Archery using Athletics and one for Firearms for further distinction..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-30T21:45:54-08:00","id":1501777,"title":"","content":"Where can I find the errata for contagion chronicles? I noticed the Promethean edge is missing from the Evolve vector.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/13.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4793-hunterinthenight","name":"HunterInTheNight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-31T05:14:02-08:00","id":1501804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HunterInTheNight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1501777#post1501777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where can I find the errata for contagion chronicles? I noticed the Promethean edge is missing from the Evolve vector.</div> </div> </div> </div>Redownload the file from <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/318347/Chronicles-of-Darkness-The-Contagion-Chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">DriveThruRPG</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-01T21:48:35-08:00","id":1501928,"title":"","content":"Hi there. Probably somebody asked this already, yet - is there conversion guide for WoD-CofD system?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-02T09:25:48-08:00","id":1501955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1501928#post1501928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Hi there. Probably somebody asked this already, yet - is there conversion guide for WoD-CofD system?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure exactly what you mean by a &quot;conversion guide,&quot; but the God-Machine Rules Update, which details all the changes between 1e and 2e's base rules, is free: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/114078/World-of-Darkness-GodMachine-Rules-Update\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...e-Rules-Update</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-02T15:27:14-08:00","id":1501988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1501928#post1501928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Hi there. Probably somebody asked this already, yet - is there conversion guide for WoD-CofD system?</div> </div> </div> </div>There has been no new conversion guide between World games and Chronicles games since the Demon Translation Guide came out. Of those, there are guides for Vampire, Werewolf, Mage, and the afore mentioned Demon. None of them deal directly with current editions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-02T23:21:32-08:00","id":1502010,"title":"","content":"What kinds of weapons do people generally use for their characters? High damage weapons tend to be big, have high Availability requirements, <i>and</i> large initiative penalties. Knives actually seem worse than brass knuckles, on top of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27777-danielxcutter","name":"danielxcutter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-03T15:28:28-08:00","id":1502054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danielxcutter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1502010#post1502010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What kinds of weapons do people generally use for their characters? High damage weapons tend to be big, have high Availability requirements, <i>and</i> large initiative penalties. Knives actually seem worse than brass knuckles, on top of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anything that is not subject to what the situation needs is usually subject to the iconics of the character. There are scenarios where shanking a person with a knife is more covert than beating them with brass knuckles, but you probably wouldn't be Johnny Teethknocker if you didn't have you some brass knuckles, as a mild example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-03T23:42:24-08:00","id":1502084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1502054#post1502054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anything that is not subject to what the situation needs is usually subject to the iconics of the character. There are scenarios where shanking a person with a knife is more covert than beating them with brass knuckles, but you probably wouldn't be Johnny Teethknocker if you didn't have you some brass knuckles, as a mild example.</div> </div> </div> </div>I said that knives were <i>worse </i>than brass knuckles - unless you have to cut something or you're throwing it, the only reasons to use one as a weapon are style and having a higher Weaponry bonus than Brawl.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27777-danielxcutter","name":"danielxcutter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T12:11:31-08:00","id":1502121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danielxcutter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1502084#post1502084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I said that knives were <i>worse </i>than brass knuckles - unless you have to cut something or you're throwing it, the only reasons to use one as a weapon are style and having a higher Weaponry bonus than Brawl.</div> </div> </div> </div>I noticed, and my argument is that that doesn't quite account for the context of game scenarios. There are points where a knife remains a better stealthy weapon than brass knuckles do, and it's important to keep that in mind because your tools depend on the context of what you're doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-11T18:36:52-08:00","id":1502802,"title":"","content":"Where might I find combat rules for eye contact?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T09:57:35-08:00","id":1502847,"title":"","content":"Is 10 the hard limit to Willpower for characters, or do supernaturals whose Composure + Resolve is beyond 10 get extra willpower dots?<br /> <br /> Is 10 the hard limit to Willpower for ephemeral entities?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T10:25:49-08:00","id":1502853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1502802#post1502802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where might I find combat rules for eye contact?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll have to find page numbers for anything that's not Nightmares from Beast, but the universal penalty in a combat situation is that eye contact is a -3 penalty\u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1502847#post1502847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is 10 the hard limit to Willpower for characters, or do supernaturals whose Composure + Resolve is beyond 10 get extra willpower dots?<br /> <br /> Is 10 the hard limit to Willpower for ephemeral entities?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no hard limit to Willpower, last I checked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T13:48:49-08:00","id":1502875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1502853#post1502853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll have to find page numbers for anything that's not Nightmares from Beast, but the universal penalty in a combat situation is that eye contact is a -3 penalty\u200b<br /> <br /> There's no hard limit to Willpower, last I checked.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Answering myself, but I found that Spirits and other ephemeral entities do have a hard limit of 10:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Werewolf Core p. 185</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Willpower: Spirits have Willpower dots equal to Resis-<br /> tance + Finesse<b>, with a maximum of ten dots for spirits of<br /> Rank 1 to 5</b>. As well as being able to gain Willpower by gorging<br /> on Essence, all spirits regain one point of Willpower per day.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage Core p. 255</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Willpower: Willpower dots are equal to Resistance + Finesse,<br /> with a<b> maximum of 10 dots for entities of Rank 1 to 5</b>. As well<br /> as the Willpower-gaining methods described above, all entities<br /> regain one point of Willpower per day\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing stated of characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T14:18:38-08:00","id":1502879,"title":"","content":"All ephemeral entities (and those who use the same rules) are capped at 10. The only other mention of a cap is in the lexicon of the base Chronicles of Darkness book, which would cap blue-book characters at 10 as well, but there's no actual mention in the rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T18:18:33-08:00","id":1502904,"title":"","content":"Boosts to WP tend to cap at 10 though, like that Promethean Alembic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27777-danielxcutter","name":"danielxcutter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-19T12:23:55-08:00","id":1503475,"title":"","content":"Do animals have souls?<br /> <br /> Do animals leave ghosts after dying?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-19T12:29:24-08:00","id":1503478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1503475#post1503475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do animals have souls?<br /> <br /> Do animals leave ghosts after dying?</div> </div> </div> </div>They don t have souls.<br /> They can leave ghosts if a human witnesses their death, the greatest the thrauma, the highest the resulting Rank","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-19T14:12:11-08:00","id":1503489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1503475#post1503475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do animals have souls?<br /> <br /> Do animals leave ghosts after dying?</div> </div> </div> </div>Humans and some humanlike beings have souls in the sense that Death magic interferes with, most notably vampires, werewolves, and changelings; deviants and mummies have human souls that are inaccessible to normal Awakened magic due to their volatility and their being the property of the Judges, respectively. Anything else's &quot;soul&quot; is part of the soul of the wider world as represented by the Anima Mundi.<br /> <br /> Ghosts can form regardless of whether the thing destroyed has a soul, and these ephemeral after-images persist outside of the Underworld until the living no longer feel loss over their absence; more information on ghosts of things other than dead humans \u2014 Castoffs, Barghests, Doppelgangers \u2014 can be found in Geist 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-31T00:58:00-07:00","id":1507029,"title":"","content":"I could have sworn that when a creature has it's right-most health box marked with lethal damage they immediately fall unconscious, but looking through the rules I can't find anything like that. In fact, since it's not bashing damage, does the creature need to roll to remain conscious at all? So, what does actually happen when the right-most health box is filled with lethal damage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-31T01:06:35-07:00","id":1507030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1507029#post1507029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could have sworn that when a creature has it's right-most health box marked with lethal damage they immediately fall unconscious, but looking through the rules I can't find anything like that. In fact, since it's not bashing damage, does the creature need to roll to remain conscious at all? So, what does actually happen when the right-most health box is filled with lethal damage?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think most creatures start bleeding to death if not given treatment ASAP, but I need to double-check on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-31T01:08:24-07:00","id":1507031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1507030#post1507030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think most creatures start bleeding to death if not given treatment ASAP, but I need to double-check on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know there's the bleeding out rule, but does the creature not fall unconscious or have to make Stamina rolls to remain conscious?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-31T01:11:45-07:00","id":1507032,"title":"","content":"Oh, I was also wondering, if something removes the 10-again quality from something, would it also remove 9-again and 8-again?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-31T04:56:43-07:00","id":1507051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1507029#post1507029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could have sworn that when a creature has it's right-most health box marked with lethal damage they immediately fall unconscious, but looking through the rules I can't find anything like that. In fact, since it's not bashing damage, does the creature need to roll to remain conscious at all? So, what does actually happen when the right-most health box is filled with lethal damage?</div> </div> </div> </div>The latest presentation of the ChroD ruleset (printed in Changeling 2e, Hunter 2e, Geist 2e, Mummy 2e, and Deviant) states outright that rolls to remains unconscious happen if you have your last Health box marked with bashing <i>or</i> lethal damage (if it's marked with aggravated damage, of course, you are dead).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-01T15:52:34-07:00","id":1507126,"title":"","content":"If your character fell into a singularity (Black Hole), would you suffer the &quot;1&quot;, and again rule for damage?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-12T13:21:21-07:00","id":1508185,"title":"","content":"Is there any kind of book comparable to Sorcerers in M20? I have ways for mortals to use influences and have a multitude of supernatural merits and minor merit templates but no actual sorcery paths or anything like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-12T13:25:13-07:00","id":1508189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1508185#post1508185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any kind of book comparable to Sorcerers in M20? I have ways for mortals to use influences and have a multitude of supernatural merits and minor merit templates but no actual sorcery paths or anything like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Without being hyper familiar with World's Sorcery, it sounds like the thaumaturgical systems from Second Sight for minor magicians, sorcerers and alchemists that have no relation to gamelines. I believe someone did an update of that system in the Storyteller's Vault called Second Sight: Third Eye. You might check both out to see if they satisfy what you're looking for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-12T13:27:37-07:00","id":1508190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1508189#post1508189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Without being hyper familiar with World's Sorcery, it sounds like the thaumaturgical systems from Second Sight for minor magicians, sorcerers and alchemists that have no relation to gamelines. I believe someone did an update of that system in the Storyteller's Vault called Second Sight: Third Eye. You might check both out to see if they satisfy what you're looking for.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have both of those and they're close I was just curious if there was anything I might have missed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-12T13:35:01-07:00","id":1508193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1508190#post1508190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have both of those and they're close I was just curious if there was anything I might have missed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hurt Locker has expanded psychics as expanded merits and merit templates, for whatever that's worth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T14:15:10-07:00","id":1509094,"title":"","content":"What skills, merits, and specialties would be appropriate for a firefighter? Also what attributes and skill categories would a firefighter focus on?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T14:29:28-07:00","id":1509098,"title":"","content":"<i>Professional Training: Firefighte</i>r, Asset Skills as Athletics and maybe Science or Survival? Specialties as &quot;Burning Envionments&quot;, &quot;Rescuing&quot;, or something similar. <i>Demolisher</i> and <i>Iron Stamina</i> would be a good merit too.<br /> <br /> Attributes would likely be Resistance stats. Skills would be Athletics, and Survival and Science would be useful. Intimidation and Brawl might be slightly stereotypical, but they'd be on-theme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 04-20-2023, 05:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T14:36:41-07:00","id":1509100,"title":"","content":"What Cauthon said, plus Weaponry wouldn\u2019t be that off for fire axe training. Above average Wits and decent empathy/persuasion for calming people down in an emergency situation, and finding people in a burning building as fast as possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T14:37:16-07:00","id":1509101,"title":"","content":"I would say strength and resistance stats would be important, weaponry could be used to wield axes to break through walls, athletics would definitely be important. After that it's going to depend on what you're doing, medicine if you have paramedic training, persuasion / subterfuge / intimidate / politics to try and climb the ladder to the upper ranks... <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T15:37:08-07:00","id":1509108,"title":"","content":"Breaking objects is a Str+Sta Attribute Task; no Weaponry required. Survival is generally for getting food or shelter, so also not applicable.<br /> <br /> I'd say Athletics &amp; Medicine and then Investigation as tertiary Asset Skill.<br /> <br /> For Attributes I would primarily focus on Strength and Stamina, followed by Wits, Composure and Resolve in roughly that order.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T16:20:35-07:00","id":1509113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1509108#post1509108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Breaking objects is a Str+Sta Attribute Task; no Weaponry required.</div> </div> </div> </div>The example breaking task is breaking out of handcuffs with nothing but your own body to aid you, that's significantly different than chopping down a wall with an axe. As a storyteller you could rule your way, but it certainly isn't a forgone conclusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T20:34:43-07:00","id":1509130,"title":"","content":"Checking my understanding of something in the Explosives mechanics, cross-checking Hurt Locker and the latest iteration of the text in Deviant: an object's Durability downgrading aggravated damage to lethal means that that damage is subject to the damage-negating effects of Durability normally, i.e. objects functionally ignore the facts that being at ground zero deals aggravated damage and Durability doesn't protect against aggravated damage, right?<br /> <br /> Otherwise Hurt Locker wouldn't have specified that any <i>remaining</i> aggravated damage bypasses Durability entirely and there'd be no point in tracking anything other than &quot;objects in the secondary blast radius effectively double their Durability against the explosion&quot; since Structure doesn't differentiate between damage types?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":".  Line break for readability. 04-20-2023, 11:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T03:10:33-07:00","id":1509155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1509130#post1509130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Checking my understanding of something in the Explosives mechanics, cross-checking Hurt Locker and the latest iteration of the text in Deviant: an object's Durability downgrading aggravated damage to lethal means that that damage is subject to the damage-negating effects of Durability normally, i.e. objects functionally ignore the facts that being at ground zero deals aggravated damage and Durability doesn't protect against aggravated damage, right?<br /> <br /> Otherwise Hurt Locker wouldn't have specified that any <i>remaining</i> aggravated damage bypasses Durability entirely and there'd be no point in tracking anything other than &quot;objects in the secondary blast radius effectively double their Durability against the explosion&quot; since Structure doesn't differentiate between damage types?</div> </div> </div> </div>You are over thinking and over complicating this. The explosive rules tell you how this works, durability downgrades a portion of the damage.damage. Also structures do not differentiate between bashing and lethal, they still take aggravated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T04:46:56-07:00","id":1509164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1509155#post1509155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are over thinking and over complicating this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am literally asking about an order of operations and explicitly doing so as a check of my understanding.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The explosive rules tell you how this works, durability downgrades a portion of the damage.damage. Also structures do not differentiate between bashing and lethal, they still take aggravated. </div> </div> </div>And I am asking if the damage that is downgraded to lethal counts as aggravated damage for the purposes of Durability's regular function, because objects downgrading damage doesn't do anything until &quot;bashing damage is completely ignored&quot; otherwise. Structure doesn't track separate damage types (it doesn't &quot;heal&quot; normally) and aggravated damage is distinguished solely by ignoring Durability; I'm asking if Durability's normal damage subtraction still applies to explosion damage after it's downgraded by the rule for how Durability applies to objects in an explosion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T08:33:43-07:00","id":1509193,"title":"","content":"Items do track aggravated and lethal separately, it may be a distinction without a difference at the moment but there is nothing in the rules as far as I can see that says to track them the same. <br /> <br /> I believe the rules for explosives supercede the normal rules for durability, it only downgrades until you're far enough out to for all the damage to be bashing. Just like with acid you wouldn't apply half the hardness then move on to the regular rules for objects and apply durability again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T14:25:20-07:00","id":1509233,"title":"","content":"I think I agree with Satchel's reading, if I'm following correctly.<br /> <br /> Say we have three objects each with Durability 2 spaced out from an explosion. The explosion deals 5 damage.<br /> <br /> At ground zero the object there is subject to 5 Aggravated damage. 2 points are downgraded to Lethal which are then absorbed by Durability and the object suffers the remaining 3 points of Aggravated.<br /> <br /> In the primary blast radius the object is subject to 5 Lethal damage. 2 points are downgraded to Bashing, 2 points are cancelled. The object takes 3 damage.<br /> <br /> In the secondary radius, the object is subject to 5 Bashing damage. 2 is downgraded to nothing, a further 2 is cancelled. The object takes 1 damage.<br /> <br /> The alternative: that the downgrading happens instead of the normal cancellation, produces damages of 5/5/3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27690-morgang","name":"MorganG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T15:41:11-07:00","id":1509236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorganG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1509233#post1509233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I agree with Satchel's reading, if I'm following correctly.<br /> <br /> Say we have three objects each with Durability 2 spaced out from an explosion. The explosion deals 5 damage.<br /> <br /> At ground zero the object there is subject to 5 Aggravated damage. 2 points are downgraded to Lethal which are then absorbed by Durability and the object suffers the remaining 3 points of Aggravated.<br /> <br /> In the primary blast radius the object is subject to 5 Lethal damage. 2 points are downgraded to Bashing, 2 points are cancelled. The object takes 3 damage.<br /> <br /> In the secondary radius, the object is subject to 5 Bashing damage. 2 is downgraded to nothing, a further 2 is cancelled. The object takes 1 damage.<br /> <br /> The alternative: that the downgrading happens instead of the normal cancellation, produces damages of 5/5/3.</div> </div> </div> </div>One way to think on the reading may boil down to if you believe the intention was to make explosives better or worse vs objects than normal methods of violence such as a punch. My reading, where hardness downgrades but doesn't remove damage, always has explosives functionally better than or equal to a punch directly to an object, while your reading has explosives equal to or less effective as an equally strong punch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T19:37:12-07:00","id":1509246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1509193#post1509193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Items do track aggravated and lethal separately, it may be a distinction without a difference at the moment but there is nothing in the rules as far as I can see that says to track them the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Each point of damage <i>removes a point of Structure</i>.&quot; You are not applying damage to Health boxes here, you are taking off points of Structure, and the only distinction is that attacks that deal aggravated damage do not subtract an object's Durability from the points of Structure they remove from the object. Objects don't heal over time or distinguish between falling unconscious/bleeding out/dying, and repairing objects harmed by aggravated damage is only harder in the sense that there will be more damage than there would be from an attack that was subject to Durability.<br /> <br /> Nothing in the rules says to track damage types the same because you don't track damage types for objects after the damage is dealt \u2014 objects respond to sources of lethal and bashing damage the same way and are more susceptible to aggravated damage, but Structure is Structure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I believe the rules for explosives supercede the normal rules for durability, it only downgrades until you're far enough out to for all the damage to be bashing. Just like with acid you wouldn't apply half the hardness then move on to the regular rules for objects and apply durability again. </div> </div> </div>That's a poor comparison, because Durability downgrading damage objects take from explosions does not involve a numerical modification of <i>the normal function of Durability</i>.<br /> <br /> If the aggravated damage being downgraded to lethal isn't otherwise subject to Durability then there is no reason to say that the damage at ground zero is downgraded at all, and your reading extends that further to every bit of damage from the explosion before the secondary blast area. Is it your contention that a Molotov cocktail \u2014 an explosive that is literally just a glass bottle full of gasoline \u2014 should be able to blow an arm-width hole in a stone wall the roughly fifty percent of the time that its Force roll comes up with a success?<br /> <br /> The system has it so that having an explosion go off within arm's reach of you is ruinous to a living body. My reading is that Durability downgrading damage \u2014 which Structure does not track differently after it's been deal \u2014 does not translate directly to objects whose Structure is less than the full damage of an explosion being vaporized by immediate proximity to the blast irrespective of their Durability, especially when Hurt Locker says that any <i>remaining</i> aggravated damage <i>ignores</i> Durability, which is what aggravated damage normally does with regards to Durability.<br /> <br /> There are already plenty of purposes for which lethal and aggravated damage are functionally the same, and I don't think damaging objects with explosives is meaningfully different from them in this way. The function of an explosive is to deal heavy damage over a large area; being able to utterly ruin a living creature at the center of the explosion doesn't translate to the same sort of impact on things that don't have organs to disrupt. Comparing it to a punch misses the fact that the main way most sources of lethal damage distinguish themselves from unarmed attacks is by having a bonus damage from a weapon, which explosives accomplish in addition to making their &quot;attack&quot; roll without accounting for Defense \u2014 I don't believe the system is intended to have all varieties of explosive be more effective at damaging an object than shooting it point-blank with an equally powerful gun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 04-21-2023, 10:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T03:01:57-07:00","id":1509265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1509236#post1509236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One way to think on the reading may boil down to if you believe the intention was to make explosives better or worse vs objects than normal methods of violence such as a punch. My reading, where hardness downgrades but doesn't remove damage, always has explosives functionally better than or equal to a punch directly to an object, while your reading has explosives equal to or less effective as an equally strong punch.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really know but here's one argument: In defence of the interpretation that explosions are less effective I'd say that explosive damage models kinetic force, heat and shrapnel spread over an area. Devastating to a person of course but a steel fence for example will easily distribute the heat; shrapnel will ricochet off; expanding gases pass through the bars etc. In contrast a sufficiently strong punch is focused in one spot (and will break most mortal hands that try it).<br /> <br /> From a design perspective there's also the point that the downgrading rule in the first scenario has two consequences: firstly that it effectively allows Durability to negate some aggravated damage and secondly that it effectively doubles Durability in the secondary radius. However if the downgrading rule replaces the usual Durability rules it only has one effect which is to say that Durability only applies to the bashing damage and not lethal. But if that was the intent why not just say that instead of talking about downgrading at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27690-morgang","name":"MorganG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T04:55:18-07:00","id":1509267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorganG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1509265#post1509265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't really know but here's one argument: In defence of the interpretation that explosions are less effective I'd say that explosive damage models kinetic force, heat and shrapnel spread over an area. Devastating to a person of course but a steel fence for example will easily distribute the heat; shrapnel will ricochet off; expanding gases pass through the bars etc. In contrast a sufficiently strong punch is focused in one spot (and will break most mortal hands that try it).</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting that you had to try very hard to find something specifically designed to fit your argument. How about a wooden table instead of a chain link fence? A chair? A wall? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> From a design perspective there's also the point that the downgrading rule in the first scenario has two consequences: firstly that it effectively allows Durability to negate some aggravated damage and secondly that it effectively doubles Durability in the secondary radius. </div> </div> </div>However, in your example the downgrading rule never actually downgrades damage. Against Agg it reduces damage to lethal, which is then absorbed by durability, in lethal it reduces it to bashing which is absorbed by durability and in bashing it doubles up. You never actually downgrades damage. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However if the downgrading rule replaces the usual Durability rules it only has one effect which is to say that Durability only applies to the bashing damage and not lethal. But if that was the intent why not just say that instead of talking about downgrading at all? </div> </div> </div>Again, this is incorrect, aggravated damage is tracked separately from lethal/bashing, so 3 Agg and 2 lethal is different than 5 Agg in theory (though perhaps not in practice). You can argue that the lack of a difference in practice is important, but I would counter that it was future proofing from the designers that just never ended up mattering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T07:52:57-07:00","id":1509275,"title":"","content":"What skills, attributes, merits, etc. would be appropriate for a paramedic? I know medicine is an obvious skill, but other specifics could I use to portray a paramedic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T08:26:58-07:00","id":1509279,"title":"","content":"Being a paramedic is a physically demanding job so athletics makes sense. Academics to represent your studies while learning medicine, maybe science. Empathy / persuasion / socialize / subterfuge for dealing with the human element of the job. Drive to get there alive. <br /> <br /> But really you could probably justify most things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T08:33:27-07:00","id":1509281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1509267#post1509267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, this is incorrect, aggravated damage is tracked separately from lethal/bashing, so 3 Agg and 2 lethal is different than 5 Agg in theory (though perhaps not in practice). You can argue that the lack of a difference in practice is important, but I would counter that it was future proofing from the designers that just never ended up mattering.</div> </div> </div> </div>It literally isn't. The closest this assertion gets to being correct is that in 1e the corebook says that Structure lost to aggravated damage can't be repaired except through supernatural powers, which 1) refers to aggravated damage as a thing <i>supernatural creatures</i> can deal, 2) has not been reproduced in any iteration of 2e's presentation of the mechanics, and 3) is never referenced, alluded to, or relied upon by any subsequent mechanic involving damaging objects thereafter.<br /> <br /> The way weapon damage works changed between editions, but we can go all the way back to Armory, where mechanics for explosives first showed up, for comparison:<br /> <br /> In 1e, damaging explosives all benefit from the Extra Successes rule on attacks (usually equal to the explosive's Force rating) and deal bashing or lethal damage; they apply their Force rating as automatic damage to anyone who isn't hit by a direct attack in with the weapon in the primary blast area and as a dicepool (which also benefits from any 8-Again or 9-Again rule the weapon applies) against anyone in the secondary radius. They can have the Armor Piercing quality, which ignores points of Armor and Durability the same even in an edition where Armor didn't do the same thing to attacks as Durability did; Thermite and White Phosphorus have AP qualities or 8 and 3, respectively, and making plastique explosives in shaped-charge form reduces their blast area but applies that reduction in yards as levels of AP. Stationary explosives that are not thrown or launched do not have a &quot;Damage&quot; rating that adds bonus dice to their attack roll (only having the extra successes the explosion applies), and instead resolve whether they hit using the systems for traps to determine whether they apply their damage or not.<br /> <br /> in 2e, damaging explosives apply their Damage rating as a type of damage determined by how close the subject is to the explosion \u2014 aggravated damage at ground zero (touching or within reach of it), lethal within the primary blast area, and bashing within the secondary blast area; they also roll their Force rating as an attack dicepool for which Defense does not usually apply against all subjects, adding successes on the roll to the damage dealt as well as applying the Damage rating again on any successful hit, applying the same type of damage by proximity as Damage does. They can have the Armor Piercing quality, which now pretty directly works the same for Armor as for Durability (the main distinctions not altering the fact that Armor Piercing attacks ignore their rating in Durability); Thermite and White Phosphorus <i>still have the same AP ratings they did in 1e</i>, despite the change in their damage numbers to account for weapon modifiers applying extra successes instead of extra dice. Objects downgrade points of damage from an explosion equal to their Durability by one level, from aggravated to lethal, lethal to bashing, and bashing to nothing; Hurt Locker says that leftover aggravated damage is not subject to Durability, which Hunter 2e reproduces and Deviant does not; presumably due to reader confusion about the definition of the term in Hurt Locker, the sidebar in Hunter clarifies &quot;ground zero&quot; as &quot;a smaller area in the explosive's immediate vicinity,&quot; while Deviant's section more directly calls it out as &quot;touching the explosive or within reach of it.&quot; Deviant is likewise the only place where it is specified that thrown explosives like grenades put the explosive within range of the primary blast radius on a successful attack roll, with an exceptional success being required for it to put the target at ground zero. Placed explosives are not given special rules.<br /> <br /> So basically, despite the edition shift, to all appearances explosives still work mostly the same after accounting for the change in how weapon damage works, and in fact explosives are <i>more</i> damaging in 2e even without the assumption that they functionally ignore Durability within the primary blast area. Setting aside for a moment the question of aggravated damage, I feel like if the intention was that being outside of ground zero of a grenade hit was enough to break most equipment on your person (dealing damage in excess of the object's Durability when most objects have Durability of 3 at most) the books would have said something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T10:31:39-07:00","id":1509300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1509246#post1509246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">cut for manageability while on phone</div> </div> </div> </div>You make a good case, especially with removing structure as opposed to tracking health boxes. <br /> <br /> And we can both make arguments of there's no reason to say downgrade the damage. For your argument they have no reason to reduce lethal to bashing, since bashing and lethal are the same. <br /> <br /> As to your molotov cocktail blowing a hole through a stone wall, let's talk about that for a minute. The Molotov cocktail is doing 3 damage. That means it can destroy a size one, durability 2 stone wall by the way I figure it. That's barely more than fits in the palm of your hand. Do I think that is possible? Generally, no, Molotov cocktails aren't typically designed to explode, they are designed to spread accelerant. But by the rules here? Sure, it's the same amount of damage a stick of dynamite would do without a success and I don't think a rock wall of that size is surviving dynamite with any regularity. <br /> <br /> I do not agree with your last point though, I do think that explosions were meant to be more destructive to structures than firearms, because realistically they are. You don't see companies dropping buildings with rifle fire. <br /> <br /> Either way I think the section is poorly written and an imperfect representation, no matter which of us is correct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T16:48:31-07:00","id":1509643,"title":"","content":"How could acid rain be represented as a tilt?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-27T03:24:02-07:00","id":1509850,"title":"","content":"An idle thought. We have the Investigation Skill, and the Investigation (sub)system. What would be a good alternative name for either?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-27T03:37:42-07:00","id":1509852,"title":"","content":"Sleuthing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-27T07:14:12-07:00","id":1509861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1509850#post1509850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An idle thought. We have the Investigation Skill, and the Investigation (sub)system. What would be a good alternative name for either?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think part of &quot;what would the rename be&quot; is going to be shaped by &quot;why do they need to be renamed&quot;. Investigation skill could be renamed searching if you're wanting to help differentiate it from the subsystem, or you could refer to the subsystem as &quot;clue finding&quot; if you're wanting to highlight that it isn't solely tied to the investigation skill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-27T14:25:08-07:00","id":1509891,"title":"","content":"I know I've seen examples of mystery cult initiation besides the basic ones in the Chronicles of Darkness book. I'd like to find the example that is like the doomsday cult or the murder cult but I cannot for the life of me seem to find them. Does anyone know what book they're in? <br /> <br /> Also, just for my peace of mind, while supernatural beings can't take supernatural merits they can be assigned them through other merits, such as mystery cult initiation, correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-27T14:32:06-07:00","id":1509892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1509891#post1509891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know I've seen examples of mystery cult initiation besides the basic ones in the Chronicles of Darkness book. I'd like to find the example that is like the doomsday cult or the murder cult but I cannot for the life of me seem to find them. Does anyone know what book they're in?<br /> <br /> Also, just for my peace of mind, while supernatural beings can't take supernatural merits they can be assigned them through other merits, such as mystery cult initiation, correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>Second Sight.<br /> <br /> And depends. Usually the supernatural community is sitting at the top and is moving the forces that cause supernatural merits, but on the other hand there are niches that suggest where the rules can be broken, most particularly how Vectors from Contagion Chronicle break the mold, so if you want to make the case that a mystery cult initiation would allow for it, I imagine no on would really say no.<br /> <br /> I mean, the answer is kind of really no, but one's going to throw you through a window if you went with it anyways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-27T14:54:52-07:00","id":1509894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1509892#post1509892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Second Sight.<br /> <br /> And depends. Usually the supernatural community is sitting at the top and is moving the forces that cause supernatural merits, but on the other hand there are niches that suggest where the rules can be broken, most particularly how Vectors from Contagion Chronicle break the mold, so if you want to make the case that a mystery cult initiation would allow for it, I imagine no on would really say no.<br /> <br /> I mean, the answer is kind of really no, but one's going to throw you through a window if you went with it anyways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. My version was in a 3PP that I guess brought some of the rules from Second Sight up but I wouldn't have checked it without you so thank you. <br /> <br /> And I agree about the supernatural community sitting at the top, but would it be weird for the leader of the cult not to have the cult merit or the cult abilities? I can kind of see it both ways. I may just brew a different cult that doesn't have the supernatural merits and bypass the issue altogether.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T08:32:24-07:00","id":1509959,"title":"","content":"Hi, this might be a strange thing to bring up, but could someone tell me how modifiers actually work, because I have a horrible feeling that a lot of people, including myself, might be doing it very wrong<br /> <br /> this is the rule from DtR and CtL <br /> <br /> Modifiers: Bonuses add the indicated number of dice; penalties remove them. Unless otherwise specified, modifiers never exceed +/\u20135. Add all bonuses before subtracting penalties.\u200b<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24579-jjbooklord42","name":"JJBooklord42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T18:21:07-07:00","id":1510008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JJBooklord42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1509959#post1509959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi, this might be a strange thing to bring up, but could someone tell me how modifiers actually work, because I have a horrible feeling that a lot of people, including myself, might be doing it very wrong<br /> <br /> this is the rule from DtR and CtL<br /> <br /> Modifiers: Bonuses add the indicated number of dice; penalties remove them. Unless otherwise specified, modifiers never exceed +/\u20135. Add all bonuses before subtracting penalties.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the idea, though the ambiguity of whether &quot;modifiers&quot; means &quot;total modifiers&quot; or &quot;individual modifiers&quot; is where a lot of the confusion seems to live; my understanding is that the intention is for you not to be able to get a non-elective Dramatic Failure on a roll whose base pool you have more than five dice in nor more than double your pool past the same threshold \u2014 rolling fifteen dice, which gives you a roughly 50% chance of rolling an Exceptional Success, is understandably meant to be the product of extremely beneficial circumstances to extremely talented and well-trained people when supernatural enhancements aren't involved.<br /> <br /> Supporting this read is the fact that Mage frames penalties for casting with additional spell factors as deviating from &quot;the normal -5 penalty cap to dice pools&quot; while not providing the same exception to bonuses from Yantras, which are explicitly capped at a net positive modifier of +5 after penalties are applied. Where people get iffy about that is the fact that in certain circumstances it's very easy to reach the point where certain circumstantial bonuses just end up going to waste, e.g. spending three Vitae to enhance a roll with Physical Intensity in Requiem, assuming the intention conveyed by the example case in the 1e corebook carries forward into 2e, would result in only five dice being added instead of six from the two per Vitae, or any changeling with Acute Senses getting a circumstantial bonus higher than [5-Wyrd], or a Paradox risk roll being composed entirely of modifiers.<br /> <br /> Presumably a later iteration or edition of the system will be fully unambiguous about it, but for the moment the intention does seem to be that the total modifiers don't exceed five dice up or down from your base pool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T21:42:48-07:00","id":1510027,"title":"","content":"What\u2019s the best way to go about converting powers from other game lines \u2014 like VtR &amp; CtL for example \u2014 to work w/ CofD rules? There\u2019s cool stuff I want to use but I don\u2019t know if my idea for switching to CofD makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27935-trynmybest","name":"trynmybest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27935_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T22:00:20-07:00","id":1510029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>trynmybest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1510027#post1510027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What\u2019s the best way to go about converting powers from other game lines \u2014 like VtR &amp; CtL for example \u2014 to work w/ CofD rules? There\u2019s cool stuff I want to use but I don\u2019t know if my idea for switching to CofD makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you mean Vampire: The Masquerade and Changeling: The Dreaming by any chance?<br /> <br /> Because, for Vampire: The Requiem and Changeling: The Lost, they all work on the same CofD platform so to speak. It\u2019s not like WoD\u2019s gamelines where all games\u2019 rules only have nominal commonalities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T23:15:21-07:00","id":1510041,"title":"","content":"No, I meant what I said\u2026 So right now I\u2019m just switching the Vitae or Glamour cost to Willpower. But I don\u2019t know what to do for Wyrd &amp; Blood Potency. Also there\u2019s a couple Kith Blessings &amp; Contracts that are fitting for the chronicle I\u2019m running but I digress.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27935,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27935-trynmybest","user":"trynmybest","date":". 04-29-2023, 02:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27935-trynmybest","name":"trynmybest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27935_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T23:47:06-07:00","id":1510042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>trynmybest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1510041#post1510041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I meant what I said\u2026 So right now I\u2019m just switching the Vitae or Glamour cost to Willpower. But I don\u2019t know what to do for Wyrd &amp; Blood Potency. Also there\u2019s a couple Kith Blessings &amp; Contracts that are fitting for the chronicle I\u2019m running but I digress.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you\u2019re scrapping out each line\u2019s monsters\u2019 unique mechanics, to run them solely via the \u2018blue book\u2019 core?<br /> <br /> You might have to build each one of them from scratch using the Horror rules in the core. (It has the Potency trait for Horrors) I don\u2019t think anybody\u2019s done that stuff yet, though. At least not here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-29T03:51:11-07:00","id":1510053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1510008#post1510008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the idea, though the ambiguity of whether &quot;modifiers&quot; means &quot;total modifiers&quot; or &quot;individual modifiers&quot; is where a lot of the confusion seems to live; my understanding is that the intention is for you not to be able to get a non-elective Dramatic Failure on a roll whose base pool you have more than five dice in nor more than double your pool past the same threshold \u2014 rolling fifteen dice, which gives you a roughly 50% chance of rolling an Exceptional Success, is understandably meant to be the product of extremely beneficial circumstances to extremely talented and well-trained people when supernatural enhancements aren't involved.<br /> <br /> Supporting this read is the fact that Mage frames penalties for casting with additional spell factors as deviating from &quot;the normal -5 penalty cap to dice pools&quot; while not providing the same exception to bonuses from Yantras, which are explicitly capped at a net positive modifier of +5 after penalties are applied. Where people get iffy about that is the fact that in certain circumstances it's very easy to reach the point where certain circumstantial bonuses just end up going to waste, e.g. spending three Vitae to enhance a roll with Physical Intensity in Requiem, assuming the intention conveyed by the example case in the 1e corebook carries forward into 2e, would result in only five dice being added instead of six from the two per Vitae, or any changeling with Acute Senses getting a circumstantial bonus higher than [5-Wyrd], or a Paradox risk roll being composed entirely of modifiers.<br /> <br /> Presumably a later iteration or edition of the system will be fully unambiguous about it, but for the moment the intention does seem to be that the total modifiers don't exceed five dice up or down from your base pool.</div> </div> </div> </div>thanks so much for answering <br /> <br /> okay so I've gone and written in three CoD discords and gotten 4-6 different answers from other players or gms to basically this, and the thought that everyone is playing the game fundamentally very differently kinda bothers me quite a lot","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24579-jjbooklord42","name":"JJBooklord42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-29T04:58:36-07:00","id":1510063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JJBooklord42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1510053#post1510053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> thanks so much for answering<br /> <br /> okay so I've gone and written in three CoD discords and gotten 4-6 different answers from other players or gms to basically this, and the thought that everyone is playing the game fundamentally very differently kinda bothers me quite a lot</div> </div> </div> </div>It may not make as much of a difference in play as you think. Might I ask what in particular bothers you about it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27690-morgang","name":"MorganG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-29T05:28:37-07:00","id":1510064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JJBooklord42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1510053#post1510053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> thanks so much for answering<br /> <br /> okay so I've gone and written in three CoD discords and gotten 4-6 different answers from other players or gms to basically this, and the thought that everyone is playing the game fundamentally very differently kinda bothers me quite a lot</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's a stretch if a couple of dice here or there under extreme situations really is &quot;very differently.&quot; But really even if it is that's ok, everyone plays every game very differently, everyone lives their lives very differently. Variety is the spice of life, and all that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-29T06:46:34-07:00","id":1510076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorganG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1510063#post1510063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It may not make as much of a difference in play as you think. Might I ask what in particular bothers you about it?</div> </div> </div> </div>That there is no clear or accepted understanding in how modifiers are applied? How can any mechanical discussions occur if one of the core parts of fundamental mathematics behind the system is played very differently in every game<br /> <br /> The versions I've seen responded include:<br /> <br /> 1) Total sum of modifiers to a pool can't exceed + or - 5 without explicit permission i.e wizard spell casting, resisted actions/ defence<br /> 2) Each bonus or penalty has a maximum of +5 or -5 and are all added or taken away from the base pool, each a separate modifier<br /> 3) All modifiers are calculated by adding related penalties and bonuses together like circumstances or magical abilities or team work (equipment is expressly this), each group not capable of exceeding +5 -5 which is then added to the dice pool<br /> 4) total end sum of each modifier can't exceed +5 or -5, but all penalties are added together and all bonuses are added together before being applied to the final pool<br /> 5) equipment and circumstances is one combined modifier, all others are separate and unique modifiers that apply<br /> 6) multiple different circumstances can apply to a pool<br /> <br /> the difference between a vampire being capped to use physical potency do boost a pool above +5 seems relevant, every interpretation implies that ability wouldn't have any advantage after you spend 2.5 vitae as its a modifier above +5. Willpower, specialities, conditions and tilts, all out attacks and called shots are all things that aren't direct boosts to attributes or skills and thus are encapsulated in these bonuses/penalty rules, and no one seems to remotely have the same answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24579-jjbooklord42","user":"JJBooklord42","date":". 04-29-2023, 09:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24579-jjbooklord42","name":"JJBooklord42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-29T18:27:23-07:00","id":1510138,"title":"","content":"Can a spirit (or other entity) use a person's supernatural merits while possessing them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-29T21:27:53-07:00","id":1510155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1510042#post1510042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So you\u2019re scrapping out each line\u2019s monsters\u2019 unique mechanics, to run them solely via the \u2018blue book\u2019 core?<br /> <br /> You might have to build each one of them from scratch using the Horror rules in the core. (It has the Potency trait for Horrors) I don\u2019t think anybody\u2019s done that stuff yet, though. At least not here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Idk what happened to my original reply bc I\u2019m not seeing it anywhere\u2026 I\u2019m running a mostly mortal chronicle - supernatural elements exist it\u2019s just not known to the players as of yet. I\u2019m not doing Dread Powers bc VtR &amp; CtL both have thematic power sets which fits w/ what me &amp; my players have in mind. Also both of those game lines have the 3 part dice pool which I like a lot bc it separates a power roll from other generic rolls. So yeah I guess I\u2019m trying to use the powers w/o the monsters mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27935-trynmybest","name":"trynmybest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27935_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T00:17:57-07:00","id":1510168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>trynmybest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1510155#post1510155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Idk what happened to my original reply bc I\u2019m not seeing it anywhere\u2026 I\u2019m running a mostly mortal chronicle - supernatural elements exist it\u2019s just not known to the players as of yet. I\u2019m not doing Dread Powers bc VtR &amp; CtL both have thematic power sets which fits w/ what me &amp; my players have in mind. Also both of those game lines have the 3 part dice pool which I like a lot bc it separates a power roll from other generic rolls. So yeah I guess I\u2019m trying to use the powers w/o the monsters mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not using Blood Potency, Vitae, etc. and yet using the three-part dice pools (which involves Discipline ratings, etc) feels a lot awkward to me...<br /> <br /> But yeah, I think you can get away with just using Potency and Willpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T00:19:04-07:00","id":1510169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1510138#post1510138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a spirit (or other entity) use a person's supernatural merits while possessing them?</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to say Yes, but I'm not seeing anything that can confirm in any direction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T06:46:03-07:00","id":1510196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1510169#post1510169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I want to say Yes, but I'm not seeing anything that can confirm in any direction.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's my problem, I feel like I read once that merits are a case by case basis, and while a spirit might benefit from some merits, like ones that increase size, they couldn't benefit from supernatural ones. But I cannot find that rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T08:20:24-07:00","id":1510202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1510196#post1510196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's my problem, I feel like I read once that merits are a case by case basis, and while a spirit might benefit from some merits, like ones that increase size, they couldn't benefit from supernatural ones. But I cannot find that rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>At the very least, way back in Mage 1e the &quot;Spirit Possession&quot; spell specified that a possessing spirit retained access to its own powers but couldn't access any of the host's paranormal abilities that aren't purely physical, with the example of a possessed ancient vampire availing its Strength score of 6 but not being able to use its telepathic abilities or supernatural allure or even to further increase its physical traits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T14:36:31-07:00","id":1510259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1510168#post1510168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not using Blood Potency, Vitae, etc. and yet using the three-part dice pools (which involves Discipline ratings, etc) feels a lot awkward to me...<br /> <br /> But yeah, I think you can get away with just using Potency and Willpower.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just feel like the Potency ranking for Horrors doesn\u2019t work for PCs\u2026 maybe that\u2019s bc Horrors are supposed to ST characters idk\u2026 I was thinking of making the 3 part dice pool consist of the following: Main Attribute + Attribute/Skill + Attribute/Skill. The Main Attribute is consistent across all the powers in a given set but the others can vary depending on the nature of the specific ability. Just for clarification here\u2019s an example of what I\u2019m thinking for something along the lines of telepathic powers\u2026<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 600px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Power: Scratch the Surface (Dot Purchase Cost: Free)<br /> Can read the surface thoughts of people nearby. They reflexively resist unless preoccupied, have low intelligence, or under stress.</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Dice Pool: Intelligence + Presence + Socialize vs target\u2019s Resolve</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Power: Mind Delver (Dot Purchase Cost: 2)<br /> Reading a person\u2019s mind in a deeper sense than just their surface thoughts. The target reflexively resists this as well.</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Dice Pool: Intelligence + Manipulation + Investigation vs target\u2019s Subterfuge + Resolve</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Power: Liar Liar (Dot Purchase Cost: 3)<br /> Peering into someone mind to see if they\u2019re telling the truth or not \u2014 exceptional success allows you to get the truth as well.\u200b</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Dice Pool: Intelligence + Intimidation + Manipulation vs target\u2019s Intelligence + Subterfuge</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Power: Plant Directive (Dot Purchase Cost: 4)<br /> Implant a specific order into your victim\u2019s mind which they must carry out no matter what \u2014 exceptional success allows you to make it delayed/conditional - coming to the forefront when certain circumstances arise.\u200b (Pre Req: Mind Delver)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Dice Pool: Intelligence + Subterfuge + Persuasion vs target\u2019s Intelligence + Resolve\u200b</td> </tr> </table></div> \u200b<br /> I don\u2019t know but it makes sense to me\u2026","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27935-trynmybest","name":"trynmybest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27935_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T14:43:52-07:00","id":1510262,"title":"","content":"This... seems like a lot more work than it's worth. Mind if I ask why you're doing it this way? CofD is fairly crossover-friendly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-04T18:22:59-07:00","id":1510745,"title":"","content":"Supposing a character was trying to make something with the intent to sell or trade it, how would one determine the Availability of the result? Build Equipment as though creating Cash springs to mind for things with no obvious direct mechanical use like art (or counterfeit money, obviously), but I don't know whether that tracks as well for things that have a practical use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-04T18:34:27-07:00","id":1510747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1510745#post1510745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Supposing a character was trying to make something with the intent to sell or trade it, how would one determine the Availability of the result? Build Equipment as though creating Cash springs to mind for things with no obvious direct mechanical use like art (or counterfeit money, obviously), but I don't know whether that tracks as well for things that have a practical use.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh\u2026 find a like product, note its typical Availability rating, and 1) subtract 1 if the character is not a professional crafter of the like product, or 2) use the rating as is if the character is indeed professional (represented by Specialties and/or the Professional Training Merit)? From there, increasing Availability would be like adding new features.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-04T18:47:02-07:00","id":1510748,"title":"","content":"Consult the bones, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-04T17:04:38-07:00","id":1513902,"title":"","content":"Has anyone seen or have ideas for a swimming style merit? I'm thinking you could adapt the parkour style mechanics (pursue,evade, dive instead of jump) but maybe there is a better way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-04T23:20:55-07:00","id":1513917,"title":"","content":"Going to probably make a thread for this as well, but is there any list of all the intertextual references and allusions in Chronicles of Darkness, or even the old new World of Darkness?<br /> <br /> Stuff like the Guardians of the Veil being behind the Aegis Kai Doru, that sort of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-04T23:59:35-07:00","id":1513920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1513917#post1513917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going to probably make a thread for this as well, but is there any list of all the intertextual references and allusions in Chronicles of Darkness, or even the old new World of Darkness?<br /> <br /> Stuff like the Guardians of the Veil being behind the Aegis Kai Doru, that sort of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Guardians of the Veil being behind the AKD is a hypothetical, not an absolute fact. ANd there's no such guide, as far as I know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-05T13:51:49-07:00","id":1513970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvinSiler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1513902#post1513902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone seen or have ideas for a swimming style merit? I'm thinking you could adapt the parkour style mechanics (pursue,evade, dive instead of jump) but maybe there is a better way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the main issue is that swimming in general does not appear to have dedicated mechanics. The Flooded environmental effect is the closest thing covering it, but nothing exemplifies water hazards, how long a character can hold their breath, what difficulties does underwater combat present and so on. What kind of focus would you like to give it ? Being able to navigate underwater areas safely (like the Gran Acuifero Maya) or , dealing with combat (shark attacks, suddenly stepping on a mantaray, etc), freediving, exploring underwater (shipwrecks, sunken cities, etc) ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-05T15:51:04-07:00","id":1513976,"title":"","content":"I was thinking it would be an Athletics based style. So the emphasis would be on freediving, navigating, exploring, and securing greater success at pursuit and evasion in a chase (There are theoretically sunken cities to explore, but we have not gotten that far in our chronicle, so who knows). Since my character is an apprentice of life, breath-holding is not the priority, since she could control oxygen metabolism or metamorphose gills with additional training in the Arcanum. At greater depths do you think Mater or Forces would apply more to water pressure?<br /> <br /> Fighting sharks (or <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quinotaur\" target=\"_blank\">other things</a>?) would be cool, but the character only has one dot in brawl and one dot in firearms so mundane combat is not her specialty (although the combat archery style from HL is intriguing). Commanding sharks to fight for her, <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/HeartIsAnAwesomePower\" target=\"_blank\">however</a>...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-05T17:37:23-07:00","id":1513979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvinSiler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1513976#post1513976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking it would be an Athletics based style. So the emphasis would be on freediving, navigating, exploring, and securing greater success at pursuit and evasion in a chase (There are theoretically sunken cities to explore, but we have not gotten that far in our chronicle, so who knows). Since my character is an apprentice of life, breath-holding is not the priority, since she could control oxygen metabolism or metamorphose gills with additional training in the Arcanum. At greater depths do you think Mater or Forces would apply more to water pressure?<br /> <br /> Fighting sharks (or <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quinotaur\" target=\"_blank\">other things</a>?) would be cool, but the character only has one dot in brawl and one dot in firearms so mundane combat is not her specialty (although the combat archery style from HL is intriguing). Commanding sharks to fight for her, <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/HeartIsAnAwesomePower\" target=\"_blank\">however</a>...</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say Forces because of Environmental Shield (pressure), Nightvision (sight in the ocean abyss) and the ability to keep a steady contact signal to the surface.<br /> <br /> I wonder if drone fighting could be repurposed so she could make a specialized underwater exploration and combat drone. Why risk it when you can scout ahead ? You can record everything, map things out, take samples, etc.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-05T23:54:34-07:00","id":1513990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1513920#post1513920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Guardians of the Veil being behind the AKD is a hypothetical, not an absolute fact. And there's no such guide, as far as I know.</div> </div> </div> </div>All the implications are just hypotheticals. But I'm still interested in learning about them.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T08:43:34-07:00","id":1514198,"title":"","content":"How strong is the demolisher merit? Like, if a character has demolisher 3, he can completly ignore a layer of steel and try to punch a door until it breaks?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T09:31:33-07:00","id":1514200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1514198#post1514198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How strong is the demolisher merit? Like, if a character has demolisher 3, he can completly ignore a layer of steel and try to punch a door until it breaks?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When damaging an object, she ignores one point of the object\u2019s Durability per dot with this Merit.\u200b </div> </div> </div>Durability is effectively an object's armor rating and Demolisher \u2022\u2022\u2022 can ignore the damage reduction of steel and iron without any reinforced layers (which add +1 Durability). So yes, given enough time and opportunity, a character could render a non-reinforced steel door unusable. As for how <i>strong</i> the Merit is, balance-wise? It's <i>very </i>useful for breaking objects and weapons and can be universally taken by any splat, but it has a three-dot Strength or Intelligence prerequisite and needs 3 XP to become as efficient as possible, so it's subjective really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23800,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23800-the-firebrand","user":"The Firebrand","date":". 06-08-2023, 12:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23800-the-firebrand","name":"The Firebrand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23800_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-21T07:18:33-07:00","id":1522891,"title":"","content":"I know as a general thing you're not supposed to be able to break the action economy in CofD. But every so often I run across something and I wonder if it is an exception to the rule or not. Some examples of this include Sin Eaters being able to unlock multiple haunts &quot;simultaneously&quot; if they have multiple copies of the same key via mementos, a vampire taking aim &quot;instantly&quot; with quicken sight, or a beast attacking twice with a regular attack and &quot;reflexive&quot; dragonfire. Do you all think those are really meant to break the action economy or are those just descriptions? (Which I can see for the first two, but the Beast one really seems like rules text.)<br /> <br /> Another example of that is the numerous abilities that allow one to make an unarmed attack and start a grapple at the same time, but they almost have to do what they say since the only thing they do is break the action economy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","user":"ShadowcatX","date":". 09-21-2023, 10:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-21T08:26:13-07:00","id":1522897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1522891#post1522891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know as a general thing you're not supposed to be able to break the action economy in CofD. But every so often I run across something and I wonder if it is an exception to the rule or not. Some examples of this include Sin Eaters being able to unlock multiple haunts &quot;simultaneously&quot; if they have multiple copies of the same key via mementos, a vampire taking aim &quot;instantly&quot; with quicken sight, or a beast attacking twice with a regular attack and &quot;reflexive&quot; dragonfire. Do you all think those are really meant to break the action economy or are those just descriptions? (Which I can see for the first two, but the Beast one really seems like rules text.)<br /> <br /> Another example of that is the numerous abilities that allow one to make an unarmed attack and start a grapple at the same time, but they almost have to do what they say since the only thing they do is break the action economy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you always do a reflexive thing the same turn you take an instant action?<br /> <br /> I meant the only example I can think of is using a yantra (apart from high speech) reflexively while casting a spell in Mage. But I don't think that breaks the action economy...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-21T08:29:05-07:00","id":1522898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1522897#post1522897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can you always do a reflexive thing the same turn you take an instant action?<br /> <br /> I meant the only example I can think of is using a yantra (apart from high speech) reflexively while casting a spell in Mage. But I don't think that breaks the action economy...</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I know, yes, you can. You get 1 instant action, 1 reflexive action, and 1 move action. At least that was the case in Werewolf the Forsaken, I assume it's standard across the board.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-21T09:34:06-07:00","id":1522903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1522898#post1522898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I know, yes, you can. You get 1 instant action, 1 reflexive action, and 1 move action. At least that was the case in Werewolf the Forsaken, I assume it's standard across the board.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. You get 1 instant action and your movement (which is not technically an action, but whatever) during your turn.<br /> <br /> You don't have a set number of reflexive actions. When you fulfil the requirements for a potential action, you can choose to take that reflexive action, during anyone's turn and without limitations. (Unless limitations are explicitly stated, like how certain reflexive actions uses up your instant action, for example.)<br /> WtF is not an exception to that. Otherwise you wouldn't be able to <b>apply your defense</b>, <b>contest a hostile power</b>, and <b>spend Essence</b> because all three of those are reflexive actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-21T10:22:30-07:00","id":1522905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1522903#post1522903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. You get 1 instant action and your movement (which is not technically an action, but whatever) during your turn.<br /> <br /> You don't have a set number of reflexive actions. When you fulfil the requirements for a potential action, you can choose to take that reflexive action, during anyone's turn and without limitations. (Unless limitations are explicitly stated, like how certain reflexive actions uses up your instant action, for example.)<br /> WtF is not an exception to that. Otherwise you wouldn't be able to <b>apply your defense</b>, <b>contest a hostile power</b>, and <b>spend Essence</b> because all three of those are reflexive actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are correct, I was misremembering. You can only activate 1 reflexive gift in a turn but you can take multiple reflexive actions. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-21T10:29:20-07:00","id":1522906,"title":"","content":"I don't think Mage has specifics written about how many reflexive spells you can cast in a turn, but they are so rare and circumstantial as to not be worth the word count.<br /> <br /> Are there reflexive powers in other games?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-21T10:29:28-07:00","id":1522907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1522891#post1522891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know as a general thing you're not supposed to be able to break the action economy in CofD. But every so often I run across something and I wonder if it is an exception to the rule or not. Some examples of this include Sin Eaters being able to unlock multiple haunts &quot;simultaneously&quot; if they have multiple copies of the same key via mementos, a vampire taking aim &quot;instantly&quot; with quicken sight, or a beast attacking twice with a regular attack and &quot;reflexive&quot; dragonfire. Do you all think those are really meant to break the action economy or are those just descriptions? (Which I can see for the first two, but the Beast one really seems like rules text.)<br /> <br /> Another example of that is the numerous abilities that allow one to make an unarmed attack and start a grapple at the same time, but they almost have to do what they say since the only thing they do is break the action economy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tessie cleared up your other misconception, so on Beast:<br /> <br /> In the case of Dragonfire, the reflexive aspect is for the ability to raise immunity towards fire and smoke-the actual fire attack is still an instant action. This is one of those things that got errata'd (pretty early, actually) but never made it into the final version because Beast's production was a bit of a shit show. Fans have been mourning the lack of clarification ever since, since it's come up a bunch.<br /> <br /> An addendum to Tessie's notation on Reflexive actions: You can take any number of reflexive actions you want in a turn, but pretty much each individual reflexive action can only be done once per turn unless the rules otherwise state.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1522905#post1522905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are correct, I was misremembering. You can only activate 1 reflexive gift in a turn but you can take multiple reflexive actions. Thank you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since I mildly addressed this, I want to group it into here as an added elaboration-you can activate any and all Reflexive Facets you have and are able to in a given turn, but you can activate each one only once.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-21-2023, 03:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-21T10:33:01-07:00","id":1522908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1522906#post1522906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think Mage has specifics written about how many reflexive spells you can cast in a turn, but they are so rare and circumstantial as to not be worth the word count.<br /> <br /> Are there reflexive powers in other games?</div> </div> </div> </div>Every single Contract in Changeling can be reflexive if you fulfill the catch and still spend the glamour/willpower costs. Demon's riddled with Reflexives.<br /> <br /> I'm going to do myself a favor and just say yes, there's reflexive actions in every game. Some games have more than others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-21T11:00:29-07:00","id":1522911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1522891#post1522891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some examples of this include Sin Eaters being able to unlock multiple haunts &quot;simultaneously&quot; if they have multiple copies of the same key via mementos,</div> </div> </div> </div>They can't unlock multiple Haunts, they can unlock multiple copies of the same Key or apply multiple Enhancements to an existing Haunt; every published Haunt is activated with an instant action.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> or a beast attacking twice with a regular attack and &quot;reflexive&quot; dragonfire. Do you all think those are really meant to break the action economy or are those just descriptions? (Which I can see for the first two, but the Beast one really seems like rules text.) </div> </div> </div>Dragonfire is activated reflexively and is resolved as a ranged attack. A ranged attack is an instant action; the Atavism is Reflexive in the same sense that a Quick Lash in Deviant is; you have a &quot;weapon&quot; that you can ready without taking a turn, but using it once it's ready is not any faster than throwing a punch.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Another example of that is the numerous abilities that allow one to make an unarmed attack and start a grapple at the same time, but they almost have to do what they say since the only thing they do is break the action economy. </div> </div> </div>Establishing a grapple uses the same dicepool as a regular melee attack; the only other thing\u200b that establishing a grapple does without an exceptional success is let you make grapple maneuvers on subsequent turns.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1522898#post1522898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I know, yes, you can. You get 1 instant action, 1 reflexive action, and 1 move action. At least that was the case in Werewolf the Forsaken, I assume it's standard across the board.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was not the case in Werewolf and it is not the case anywhere that you are limited in the number of reflexive actions you can take purely due to their being reflexive actions; reflexive actions include contesting supernatural powers you are the target of, and Werewolf includes a few things that are reflexive actions that can explicitly only be taken once per turn, which would be redundant if such a limit applied.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-21T11:42:57-07:00","id":1522912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1522911#post1522911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They can't unlock multiple Haunts, they can unlock multiple copies of the same Key or apply multiple Enhancements to an existing Haunt; every published Haunt is activated with an instant action.</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 132 under strange mementos, &quot;Sin-Eaters who collect many Mementos with the same Key can use them to unlock several Haunts with that Key simultaneously taking full advantage of resonance to combine multiple potent effects\u200b\u200b&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm just unsure if that means &quot;in the same action&quot; or if it means &quot;you can have boneyard unlocked with the key, then use the same key from a different memento to unlock caul a turn later, and then the turn after that use yet another memento to unlock rage.&quot; I have a minor quibble with the use of the word simultaneously being applied to the unlocking (since unlocking is a specific activity done when the power is used and not something continuous) if it's the latter, but that does seem better balanced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-21T12:52:55-07:00","id":1522917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1522912#post1522912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Page 132 under strange mementos, &quot;Sin-Eaters who collect many Mementos with the same Key can use them to unlock several Haunts with that Key simultaneously taking full advantage of resonance to combine multiple potent effects\u200b\u200b&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm just unsure if that means &quot;in the same action&quot; or if it means &quot;you can have boneyard unlocked with the key, then use the same key from a different memento to unlock caul a turn later, and then the turn after that use yet another memento to unlock rage.&quot; I have a minor quibble with the use of the word simultaneously being applied to the unlocking (since unlocking is a specific activity done when the power is used and not something continuous) if it's the latter, but that does seem better balanced.</div> </div> </div> </div>The latter. I'll have to reread when I'm not busy, but I believe it's talking about the resonance benefit for Keys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-21T13:39:10-07:00","id":1522918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1522912#post1522912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 132 under strange mementos, &quot;Sin-Eaters who collect many Mementos with the same Key can use them to unlock several Haunts with that Key simultaneously taking full advantage of resonance to combine multiple potent effects\u200b\u200b&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm just unsure if that means &quot;in the same action&quot; or if it means &quot;you can have boneyard unlocked with the key, then use the same key from a different memento to unlock caul a turn later, and then the turn after that use yet another memento to unlock rage.&quot; I have a minor quibble with the use of the word simultaneously being applied to the unlocking (since unlocking is a specific activity done when the power is used and not something continuous) if it's the latter, but that does seem better balanced.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the latter. It's saying you can use Mementos with the same Key to unlock multiple Haunts because the normal state of affairs is that if you use a Key to unlock a Haunt that Key is unusable until you resolve its Doom. Every other part of the game's mechanics agrees that activating a Haunt is an instant action; it's purely supplementary elements of doing so, like activating Enhancements or using a Key to unlock it for extra dice and Plasm, that are reflexive actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-12T05:18:47-08:00","id":1530634,"title":"","content":"Can Psychic Vampire still cause damage even if they just only steal Willpower?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-12T06:37:12-08:00","id":1530638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1530634#post1530634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Psychic Vampire still cause damage even if they just only steal Willpower?</div> </div> </div> </div>If they use a gun they could, but not with their merit. With the merit they can only steal willpower from a vampire, and stealing willpower doesn't do damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-12T18:52:40-08:00","id":1530695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1530634#post1530634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Psychic Vampire still cause damage even if they just only steal Willpower?</div> </div> </div> </div>Until the fifth dot in the core Merit, you are specifically choosing one or the other when you attempt to siphon Ephemera from another character, and at the fifth dot you have the option to do both at once. If you're only doing the one, you are specifically not doing the other, so no, if you are only stealing Willpower you are not dealing damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-13T06:14:49-08:00","id":1530737,"title":"","content":"I could have sworn there was an option to start with a persistent condition in the books, but I can't seem to find it. Am I mistaken?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-13T07:59:20-08:00","id":1530742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1530737#post1530737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could have sworn there was an option to start with a persistent condition in the books, but I can't seem to find it. Am I mistaken?</div> </div> </div> </div>The God-Machine Chronicle, p. 180:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Some Conditions are marked as Persistent. These Conditions are tied inexorably to the character (replacing the Flaws in the World of Darkness Rulebook). Persistent Conditions may offer one Beat per game session when they complicate the character\u2019s life. With Storyteller permission, players may take Persistent Conditions for their characters at character creation. Persistent Conditions may be resolved permanently only with a specific and impressive effort, along with Storyteller discretion. </div> </div> </div>Subsequent books, including the Chronicles of Darkness Rulebook, appear to have forgotten or omitted this text.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-13T10:12:17-08:00","id":1530748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1530742#post1530742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The God-Machine Chronicle, p. 180:<br /> <br /> Subsequent books, including the Chronicles of Darkness Rulebook, appear to have forgotten or omitted this text.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you so much. That was driving me nuts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-13T20:28:38-08:00","id":1530777,"title":"","content":"Just rewatching Anime Erased and wondered how difficult is it to detect spousal or child abuse fr om incidental signs","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avat