orum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-28T00:22:49-08:00","id":1531668,"title":"","content":"Can you have Multiple Specialtie in one skill? And can you add bonus from multiple specialtie?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-28T02:44:49-08:00","id":1531671,"title":"","content":"The answers are on page 73 of the CofD core.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1531668#post1531668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you have Multiple Specialtie in one skill?</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And can you add bonus from multiple specialtie? </div> </div> </div>Yes, with Storyteller permission.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-28T02:48:29-08:00","id":1531672,"title":"","content":"Is there anything I need to convert, to have Thaumaturge in Chronicle of Darkness?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-28T05:26:13-08:00","id":1531675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1531672#post1531672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there anything I need to convert, to have Thaumaturge in Chronicle of Darkness?</div> </div> </div> </div>The first thing you need to do is work on what you mean by Thaumaturge. The word itself means a worker of wonders and miracles. Is that what you mean? If so, the basic book has stuff like abjuration and banishing. <br /> <br /> If you mean a Tremere esque Blood Mage, Requiem has 2 types of blood magic you can pick between, the holy Cruac and the abominable Theban Sorcery. Take either one and congrats, you're a blood mage. <br /> <br /> I think Second Sight: Third Eye has a minor templates that expands on supernatural merits called thaumaturge as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T02:46:29-08:00","id":1531772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1531675#post1531675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The first thing you need to do is work on what you mean by Thaumaturge. The word itself means a worker of wonders and miracles. Is that what you mean? If so, the basic book has stuff like abjuration and banishing.<br /> <br /> If you mean a Tremere esque Blood Mage, Requiem has 2 types of blood magic you can pick between, the holy Cruac and the abominable Theban Sorcery. Take either one and congrats, you're a blood mage.<br /> <br /> I think Second Sight: Third Eye has a minor templates that expands on supernatural merits called thaumaturge as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Requiem also has the Sons of Phobos, who teach their own version of blood sorcery, but don't require the user to become a vampire first.<br /> <br /> In which case you can have a mortal thaumaturge.<br /> <br /> Alternatively Mummy has a system for mortal sorcery, which may or may not be powered by blood, depending on the specific rituals you learn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T14:37:55-08:00","id":1531809,"title":"","content":"I am wondering, in the Chronicles of Darkness, there is the Integrity trait for mortals. In almost all other rulebooks, there are some very nasty effects of having low Humanity / extreme Harmony / low Wisdom, etc. Are there any mechanical disadvantages of low Integrity, or is it only something to be roleplayed, without mechanic effects?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24286-irigi","name":"irigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24286_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T14:56:44-08:00","id":1531811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>irigi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1531809#post1531809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am wondering, in the Chronicles of Darkness, there is the Integrity trait for mortals. In almost all other rulebooks, there are some very nasty effects of having low Humanity / extreme Harmony / low Wisdom, etc. Are there any mechanical disadvantages of low Integrity, or is it only something to be roleplayed, without mechanic effects?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lower Integrity penalizes breaking points, thus increasing your likelihood of failure/decreasing your odds of exceptional success and thereby causing you to acquire negative Conditions more easily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T02:12:29-08:00","id":1531869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1531811#post1531811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lower Integrity penalizes breaking points, thus increasing your likelihood of failure/decreasing your odds of exceptional success and thereby causing you to acquire negative Conditions more easily.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! From my understanding, on failure or success on Breaking Point, the character typically gets Guilty, Shaken, or Spooked conditions, that are quite temporary. Exceptional successes are rare. So the main disadvantage probably is increased probability of Dramatic Failure, and thus gaining serious permanent condition? (Other than that, the Integrity does not affect the daily life of the character, correct?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24286-irigi","name":"irigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24286_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T02:36:03-08:00","id":1531872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1531675#post1531675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The first thing you need to do is work on what you mean by Thaumaturge. The word itself means a worker of wonders and miracles. Is that what you mean? If so, the basic book has stuff like abjuration and banishing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean Thaumaturge from the original second sight.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T05:24:45-08:00","id":1531875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1531872#post1531872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean Thaumaturge from the original second sight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then it is updated in Second Sight Third Eye.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T05:26:34-08:00","id":1531876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>irigi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1531869#post1531869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you! From my understanding, on failure or success on Breaking Point, the character typically gets Guilty, Shaken, or Spooked conditions, that are quite temporary. Exceptional successes are rare. So the main disadvantage probably is increased probability of Dramatic Failure, and thus gaining serious permanent condition? (Other than that, the Integrity does not affect the daily life of the character, correct?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Integrity is primarily a roleplaying tool. The daily life of someone at integrity 1 and integrity 10 probably look significantly different, despite it not playing more of a mechanical role.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-11T10:25:46-07:00","id":1532380,"title":"","content":"For Grappling and the Giant/Small-Frame merits, would size add a bonus to grappling rolls? Ex: Giant char (size 6) initiates a grapple against a normal human (size 5), shouldn\u2019t the Giant get a +1 bonus to that roll? (Or a -1 if against a Giant char)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28143-firestar001","name":"firestar001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-11T13:45:20-07:00","id":1532390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>firestar001</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1532380#post1532380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Grappling and the Giant/Small-Frame merits, would size add a bonus to grappling rolls? Ex: Giant char (size 6) initiates a grapple against a normal human (size 5), shouldn\u2019t the Giant get a +1 bonus to that roll? (Or a -1 if against a Giant char)</div> </div> </div> </div>I see nothing in the grapple rules to give you a reason to think this. Where are you getting the idea?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-12T02:57:17-07:00","id":1532427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1532390#post1532390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see nothing in the grapple rules to give you a reason to think this. Where are you getting the idea?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mainly the idea of a giant and a small framed character grappling. I\u2019m just thinking \u201cshouldn\u2019t there be SOME mechanical benefit or something, or am I just overthinking this?\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28143-firestar001","name":"firestar001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-12T06:17:16-07:00","id":1532434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>firestar001</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1532427#post1532427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mainly the idea of a giant and a small framed character grappling. I\u2019m just thinking \u201cshouldn\u2019t there be SOME mechanical benefit or something, or am I just overthinking this?\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>You're over thinking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-12T10:17:40-07:00","id":1532441,"title":"","content":"Storyteller's always free to apply circumstantial dice modifiers if an action seems easier or harder. Size doesn't factor into the grappling rules, but if the action is such that it feels like it should be easier for the larger character, go ahead anyway. Probably wouldn't give it more than +1 or +2, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-21T10:10:25-07:00","id":1532946,"title":"","content":"It's possible for a Beast accidently create a prometean when creating a horrorspawn?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-21T10:56:01-07:00","id":1532948,"title":"","content":"For a non-Promethean to make one of the Created, they have to seize the Divine Fire through obsession alone, a fervid and desperate single-minded snatching for an impossible miracle.<br /> A Beast creates a Horrorspawn by following one of a couple different consistent procedures which have been established to work fairly reliably.<br /> A Beast could probably create a Promethean because more or less anyone potentially <i>can,</i> but the process wouldn't involve any of its Begotten powers, and while the intent might not be a Promethean specifically, it would have to be an intentional attempt to create an independent living being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 03-21-2024, 01:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T07:07:03-07:00","id":1533167,"title":"","content":"Are there any guidelines for handling &quot;background&quot; merits, especially magical equipment/resources, post character creation? (I haven't actually played an classic WoD, but I know the term). I've looked through multiple and I don't think any of them has given any.<br /> <br /> For example, what if a Geist player wanted an Memento that did xyz and has the experiences to buy one? Could they buy it between sessions without having to struggle? On the same topic, what about finding such an object during gameplay? Would they get the item for free? Obviously, i know it wouldn't be protected by the Sanctity of Merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28417-fae_tail","name":"Fae_Tail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28417_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T08:00:10-07:00","id":1533170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fae_Tail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1533167#post1533167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, what if a Geist player wanted an Memento that did xyz and has the experiences to buy one? Could they buy it between sessions without having to struggle? On the same topic, what about finding such an object during gameplay? Would they get the item for free? Obviously, i know it wouldn't be protected by the Sanctity of Merits.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no explicit rules for gaining Merits with Experiences besides the prerequisites and restrictions listed in individual Merits, though being able to provide narrative justification for them is understandably common.<br /> <br /> Picking up an item in play doesn't require spending Experiences unless the rules for that item say otherwise, so yes, you could e.g. find a Memento in play that has effects you want to make use of &quot;for free,&quot; with the caveats of no Sanctity of Merits and no expectation that such a thing will be guaranteed the exact qualities you'd want the way you would if you picked/designed it, had it approved by the ST, and purchased it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-28T02:53:37-07:00","id":1533304,"title":"","content":"Guess there isn't anything to go by. Thanks anyways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28417-fae_tail","name":"Fae_Tail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28417_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-01T04:49:09-07:00","id":1533450,"title":"","content":"One way of looking at it is if you find an item in play it isn't &quot;yours&quot; unless you pay for it.<br /> <br /> So just assume you can use it for one session and in between sessions it is lost (unless you have the XP to keep it).<br /> <br /> That said, this may be overly harsh. It is a story telling game, not a strict mechanical simulation. If the narrative benefits from having the item, then keeping it may be justified, if you roll a dramatic failure and the item breaks that might also suit the narrative.<br /> <br /> Edit: I would recommend talking to your Storyteller to find out how they want to run it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 04-01-2024, 07:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-01T07:33:11-07:00","id":1533453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1533450#post1533450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One way of looking at it is if you find an item in play it isn't &quot;yours&quot; unless you pay for it.<br /> <br /> So just assume you can use it for one session and in between sessions it is lost (unless you have the XP to keep it).<br /> <br /> That said, this may be overly harsh. It is a story telling game, not a strict mechanical simulation. If the narrative benefits from having the item, then keeping it may be justified, if you roll a dramatic failure and the item breaks that might also suit the narrative.<br /> <br /> Edit: I would recommend talking to your Storyteller to find out how they want to run it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems to be a very bad way to do a storytelling game to me. If an item being in the chronicle doesn't benefit the narrative the Storyteller shouldn't have introduced it to the chronicle. <br /> <br /> Also, if an item is found by a PC and becomes important to them, arbitrarily taking it away between game sessions as a punishment for them not having XP to burn at any given moment seems to lead to very poor game play, IMO. <br /> <br /> If something needs to be removed from the game between game sessions a conversation should happen between the player and the storyteller.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-02T07:24:39-07:00","id":1533482,"title":"","content":"Put the fiction first. If you made a friend then you have a friend. If there are useful mechanics for what having a friend does that make sense to apply then apply them.<br /> <br /> Merits on your sheet are protected by story insurance. You've invested in having these things and by doing so told the Storyteller &quot;don't plan to take these away, I care about my character having these.&quot; Stuff you've acquired that you haven't invested Merit dots in is not protected by story insurance. You could lose it tomorrow if the fiction calls for it and would not be compensated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-07T13:40:40-07:00","id":1533766,"title":"","content":"What happens if a Mage uses the Spirit arcana on a Promethean or a Beast, which in theory do not have a soul or in a Deviant who has a cracked soul?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-07T14:23:47-07:00","id":1533769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1533766#post1533766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens if a Mage uses the Spirit arcana on a Promethean or a Beast, which in theory do not have a soul or in a Deviant who has a cracked soul?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not generally a Mage person, but I don't think Spirit typically deals with the soul in general. Is there something specific you were planning that targets a person but uses spirit?<br /> <br /> The suggested ones in the book like Shadow Scream would work normally on a Beast or the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","user":"ShadowcatX","date":". 04-07-2024, 05:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-07T16:00:24-07:00","id":1533772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1533769#post1533769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not generally a Mage person, but I don't think Spirit typically deals with the soul in general. Is there something specific you were planning that targets a person but uses spirit?<br /> <br /> The suggested ones in the book like Shadow Scream would work normally on a Beast or the like.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't plan anything specific, I just wondered what this Arcana would do with something that doesn't have a soul in the conventional way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T02:06:26-07:00","id":1533800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1533772#post1533772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't plan anything specific, I just wondered what this Arcana would do with something that doesn't have a soul in the conventional way.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a weird question because it implies Spirit has some special interaction with those that do have conventional souls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T04:35:22-07:00","id":1533804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1533772#post1533772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't plan anything specific, I just wondered what this Arcana would do with something that doesn't have a soul in the conventional way.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is really a Mage questions n, but the answer is &quot;does the target have a spirit&quot; - a sword with an associated sword spirit (whether a rank 0 mote or higher) can be influenced by Spirit magics.<br /> <br /> I would say Deviants and Prometheans don't have spirits. Deviants still have souls, Prometheans may be made of things which had spirits (or not) but they are new things with Azoth.<br /> <br /> I don't think Goetia have spirits either, but might he more susseptible, but I don't have any interest in Beast...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-09T08:53:09-07:00","id":1533889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1533766#post1533766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens if a Mage uses the Spirit arcana on a Promethean or a Beast, which in theory do not have a soul or in a Deviant who has a cracked soul?</div> </div> </div> </div>Very little, since they\u2019re not spirits, regardless of souls or lack thereof. Death is the Arcana that deals with souls. The Contagion Chronicle Player\u2019s Guide confirms Prometheans and Beasts do not have souls. Hence Death magic can\u2019t affect them in that way. Mind with conjectural Spirit could theoretically do some shenanigans with a Beast\u2019s horror, which they have in place of a soul. Otherwise, Spirit can\u2019t do much directly to Prometheans, Beasts, or Deviants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-09T19:43:12-07:00","id":1533925,"title":"","content":"I'm reading Second Sight and I'm confused on what does Magical Ritual does?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T05:09:36-07:00","id":1533954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1533925#post1533925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm reading Second Sight and I'm confused on what does Magical Ritual does?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure I understand the question. The &quot;Magical Rituals&quot; section of Second Sight describes the basic rules for gaining the benefits of those Thaumaturge Merits that include &quot;Ritual Length&quot; and &quot;Ritual Details&quot; elements. They're the game mechanics for performing the magical rituals described in the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T05:23:23-07:00","id":1533955,"title":"","content":"Does this mean you could only do ritual for the Merit that you own?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T06:41:42-07:00","id":1533962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1533955#post1533955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does this mean you could only do ritual for the Merit that you own?</div> </div> </div> </div>As described in the first paragraph of the Thaumaturge Merits section, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T07:04:26-07:00","id":1533967,"title":"","content":"What make Thaumaturge merit more special than other Supernatural Merit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T07:23:53-07:00","id":1533970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1533967#post1533967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What make Thaumaturge merit more special than other Supernatural Merit?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're Merits you need the thaumaturge template for. Being a thaumaturge means adhering to a particular ritual tradition and the powers available to a tradition mechanically define it. It has nothing to do with &quot;more special&quot;; you may as well ask what makes Haven more special than other Safe Place modifications or alternatives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T07:32:56-07:00","id":1533972,"title":"","content":"Is there any more resource for Thaumaturge fan-made or otherwise?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T13:35:06-07:00","id":1533997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1533972#post1533972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any more resource for Thaumaturge fan-made or otherwise?</div> </div> </div> </div>Chris Falco made a <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/260310/Second-Sight-Third-Eye\" target=\"_blank\">fan-update to Second Sight</a> some years ago, but official Chronicles of Darkness books are largely made to be usable with only corebooks as separate reference material, with some exceptions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-11T15:11:15-07:00","id":1534052,"title":"","content":"Can a character have more than one specialty in a skill ? An example would be a doctor that has field medicine and medicine synthesis as his specialties. One would imagine its possible, but its also likely having only one specialty would make characters focus on a niche. As far as I could see, the CofD core book does not have a ruling on this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-11T15:46:57-07:00","id":1534057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1534052#post1534052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a character have more than one specialty in a skill ? An example would be a doctor that has field medicine and medicine synthesis as his specialties. One would imagine its possible, but its also likely having only one specialty would make characters focus on a niche. As far as I could see, the CofD core book does not have a ruling on this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Under Skill Specialties (page 73 in the Core book): &quot;A character may have any number of Specialties for a given Skill, but only one instance of each Specialty.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-11T16:05:33-07:00","id":1534060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1534057#post1534057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Under Skill Specialties (page 73 in the Core book): &quot;A character may have any number of Specialties for a given Skill, but only one instance of each Specialty.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome, thank you. I was wondering what would happen if you got more specialties from Professional Training, but you already had them for the skill. So you just get more variety, sounds good to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-14T01:11:16-07:00","id":1535546,"title":"","content":"What are the color of each of Cofd gameline?<br /> Main (Mortal): Blue<br /> Vampire: Red<br /> Werewolf: Orange? Brown?<br /> Mage: Different shade of Blue.<br /> Promethean: White? Grey? Purple?<br /> Changeling: Green<br /> Hunter: Different shade of Green<br /> Geist: Different shade of Blue<br /> Beast: Purple<br /> Demon: Black<br /> Mummy: Yellow<br /> Deviant: Different shade of Red.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-17T03:53:42-07:00","id":1535762,"title":"","content":"This is probably a dumb question, but I'm coming back to CofD after a long time away, and one of my players is interested in playing a grappling character. Therefore, my question is, what does the rulebook mean by an 'overpower maneuver'? Is that the same thing as the moves a grapple offers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-17T04:37:05-07:00","id":1535764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1535762#post1535762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is probably a dumb question, but I'm coming back to CofD after a long time away, and one of my players is interested in playing a grappling character. Therefore, my question is, what does the rulebook mean by an 'overpower maneuver'? Is that the same thing as the moves a grapple offers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, the 1e corebook explicitly uses that term in the grappling rules and there's 2e Merits dating back to the God-Machine Chronicle Rules Update (meant to be used alongside the 1e corebook) that still reference that terminology and didn't get their verbiage updated to account for the 2e presentation of the rules not using that term.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nWoD 1e Core Rulebook, p38, Roll and Trait Summary</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Grapple: Roll Strength + Brawl - opponent\u2019s Defense for attacker to get a grip on target; roll Strength + Brawl - opponent\u2019s Strength to perform an overpowering maneuver or to break free; instant action. (p. 157)</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nWoD 1e Core Rulebook, p157, Unarmed Combat - Grapple</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If in the next turn the attacker still has a hold, he can try to overpower his opponent. A Strength + Brawl roll is made. The target\u2019s Strength rather than Defense is subtracted from the attacker\u2019s dice pool. If no successes are gained, the attacker still has a hold, but accomplishes nothing more in the turn (he does not overpower his victim). If even one success is gained, one of the following overpowering maneuvers can be accomplished in the turn.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nWoD 1e Core Rulebook, 159, Sidebar: Grappling Summary</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If the attacker\u2019s grip on the target persists, and he is free to do so, the attacker can try to apply an overpowering maneuver to the victim. Roll the attacker\u2019s Strength + Brawl - opponent\u2019s Strength. Any successes allow a maneuver (see below).<br /> \u2022 Possible maneuvers. Choose one:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Render opponent prone<br /> Damage opponent<br /> Immobilize opponent<br /> Draw weapon<br /> Attack with drawn weapon<br /> Turn a drawn weapon Disarm opponent<br /> Use opponent as protection from ranged attacks</div> <br /> Attempting to break free is always an option instead of performing an overpowering maneuver.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-17T06:52:14-07:00","id":1535768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1535762#post1535762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is probably a dumb question, but I'm coming back to CofD after a long time away, and one of my players is interested in playing a grappling character. Therefore, my question is, what does the rulebook mean by an 'overpower maneuver'? Is that the same thing as the moves a grapple offers?</div> </div> </div> </div>This appears to be a product of rules text that was written based on either the 1e World of Darkness Rulebook or an earlier draft of the 2e rules that didn't get revised when the final 2e rules failed to specify what overpowering is.<br /> <br /> It's the same thing as the moves a grapple offers, the maneuvers on pp. 89-90 of the Chronicles of Darkness Rulebook (or wherever grappling rules are in your monster corebook). The 1e corebook referred to these as &quot;overpowering grappling maneuvers.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-17T11:06:57-07:00","id":1535777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1535762#post1535762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is probably a dumb question, but I'm coming back to CofD after a long time away, and one of my players is interested in playing a grappling character. Therefore, my question is, what does the rulebook mean by an 'overpower maneuver'? Is that the same thing as the moves a grapple offers?</div> </div> </div> </div>As a warning, do note that grappling can be extremely powerful as it forces the opponent to use a specific dice pool and lose access to basically all non-grappling fighting styles. There's ways to work around this as an ST, but most ways would instead overly punish the grappler. Just something to be aware of if you have combat heavy games or if that player tend to min-max.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-21T05:39:23-07:00","id":1536053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1535777#post1535777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As a warning, do note that grappling can be extremely powerful as it forces the opponent to use a specific dice pool and lose access to basically all non-grappling fighting styles. There's ways to work around this as an ST, but most ways would instead overly punish the grappler. Just something to be aware of if you have combat heavy games or if that player tend to min-max.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did encounter that issue in a previous game, and I'm using a slight houserule that makes it so that the person trying to get out of a Grapple can use Dexterity + Athletics or Brawl as well to escape, to make it a little easier to counter with more varied character types.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-26T06:14:44-07:00","id":1536293,"title":"","content":"For Atariya All-In merit, do the automatic success matter if you fail?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-26T07:21:27-07:00","id":1536298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1536293#post1536293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Atariya All-In merit, do the automatic success matter if you fail?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, hence the Merit saying &quot;a successful roll&quot; achieves additional automatic successes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-02T14:13:55-07:00","id":1536716,"title":"","content":"I have been paying more attention to a different (dead) game line the last several months (and have a knack for obliviousness), and managed to just now discover that CoD seems to have effectively been ended as a game line due to lack of support from Paradox (please correct me if I am confused).<br /> How does this affect community content? Does Paradox have to sign off on everything that shows up as community content on DrivethruRpg? I have gotten some good supplements (IMO anyway) from that source, and wonder if it is likely to dry up as well.<br /> <br /> Edited for effect","signature":"","edited":{"userid":532,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","user":"Newes","date":". 06-02-2024, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-03T17:29:42-07:00","id":1536773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1536716#post1536716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have been paying more attention to a different (dead) game line the last several months (and have a knack for obliviousness), and managed to just now discover that CoD seems to have effectively been ended as a game line due to lack of support from Paradox (please correct me if I am confused).<br /> How does this affect community content? Does Paradox have to sign off on everything that shows up as community content on DrivethruRpg? I have gotten some good supplements (IMO anyway) from that source, and wonder if it is likely to dry up as well.<br /> <br /> Edited for effect</div> </div> </div> </div>Community content is somewhat safer because of the Storyteller Vault and its rules, although they tend to also slower with time if things remain like they're now for long.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-03T18:04:26-07:00","id":1536776,"title":"","content":"Do you need to have the Asset skills at any minimum rating to take the <b>Professional Training </b>merit?<br /> <br /> Specially for starting characters, if I am thinking it right as a math optimization exercise, the idea would be to start with 0 dots on the Asset skills, and spend at least 4 merit dots to get the 3rd and 4th abilities. 3rd gives you a third Asset skill and two specialties (which should be on hold until you buy the skill dots) and 4th gives you a beat every time you purchase a dot on the Asset skills.<br /> <br /> Does my analysis make sense? Besides the ST disallowing it, is there any reason why this shouldn't work as described?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-03T22:03:23-07:00","id":1536784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1536776#post1536776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does my analysis make sense? Besides the ST disallowing it, is there any reason why this shouldn't work as described?</div> </div> </div> </div>The rulebooks aren't written like programming manuals. They're written assuming a degree of shared consensus as to what the rules are for and that some degree of common sense can be used. In the case of Professional Training, the Merit designed to represent &quot;you are invested in the practice of a particular field and active enough in its practice to cultivate networking connections,&quot; I think it's pretty evident that declaring that the skills most relevant to your field of focus (which, at four dots, you are very heavily focused and well established in) are skills that you have no practice or training in so that you can conjure maybe like five beats or so is not an intended use of this Merit, nor enriching to the game experience.<br /> <br /> Professional Training is there as low-hanging fruit to encourage you to give some definition to your character's everyday life experience and help work it into play. This is doing the opposite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-12T19:49:14-07:00","id":1537288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1536776#post1536776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you need to have the Asset skills at any minimum rating to take the <b>Professional Training </b>merit?<br /> <br /> Specially for starting characters, if I am thinking it right as a math optimization exercise, the idea would be to start with 0 dots on the Asset skills, and spend at least 4 merit dots to get the 3rd and 4th abilities. 3rd gives you a third Asset skill and two specialties (which should be on hold until you buy the skill dots) and 4th gives you a beat every time you purchase a dot on the Asset skills.<br /> <br /> Does my analysis make sense? Besides the ST disallowing it, is there any reason why this shouldn't work as described?</div> </div> </div> </div>Everything Stupid Loserman said. <br /> Take note, that &quot;specialties being on hold&quot; is not supported by any text.<br /> <br /> Now from min-maxing perspective - consider this, unless you're playing mortals - your tactic means you're now planning to spend XP on skills, which is rarely as useful as buying whatever supernatural advantages available to you. The splat benefits are much more powerful, and if you're investing in these, you're just holding on ~4 merit dots for some future. <br /> <br /> Overall, even if a ST allowed this, it's quite a waste. Instead, look at Sympathetic, which gives you conditions that you can resolve for Beats, or Inspiring (although, you'll need a friend to take this to give you Beats <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) <br /> <br /> The merit shines due to making thing your asset skills, and giving you tie ins with the world via contacts and the like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-13T20:54:08-07:00","id":1537331,"title":"","content":"Meh, I wouldn't fret too much if a player of mine tried to game Professional Training like that.<br /> <br /> For one, I don't think it that unthinkable. Every profession, specially when practiced within an organization, like a corporation, has its share of social butterflies whose success comes precisely from their ability, or sheer luck, on making the right contacts, instead of any actual ability to do their actual job.<br /> <br /> Such extremes as to not have a single dot are certainly rare but not impossible.<br /> <br /> Other than that, if the player thinks that this is earning them a lot of benefits... Why step on their dreams.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-14T05:07:03-07:00","id":1537336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1537331#post1537331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meh, I wouldn't fret too much if a player of mine tried to game Professional Training like that.<br /> <br /> For one, I don't think it that unthinkable. Every profession, specially when practiced within an organization, like a corporation, has its share of social butterflies whose success comes precisely from their ability, or sheer luck, on making the right contacts, instead of any actual ability to do their actual job.<br /> <br /> Such extremes as to not have a single dot are certainly rare but not impossible.<br /> <br /> Other than that, if the player thinks that this is earning them a lot of benefits... Why step on their dreams.</div> </div> </div> </div>4 dice pool for ([attribute 5] - 1 unskilled) should work well enough for some jobs.<br /> <br /> Especially a player character who can spend willpower on it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-14T05:37:45-07:00","id":1537338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1537336#post1537336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4 dice pool for ([attribute 5] - 1 unskilled) should work well enough for some jobs.<br /> <br /> Especially a player character who can spend willpower on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>so someone as talented and strong/smart/whatever as to be at PEAK human condition, so talented beyond belief, goes down a career path where they have 0 skills, and manage to stay on that career path long enough to build up Professional Training to 4 dots, but yet fail to pick up a single dot of relevant skills? <br /> <br /> I've seen some blatant min-maxing from my players, and it's fine, but c'mon, at least keep the characters story arc believable alongside their traits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-14T13:00:09-07:00","id":1537351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1536776#post1536776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you need to have the Asset skills at any minimum rating to take the <b>Professional Training </b>merit?<br /> <br /> Specially for starting characters, if I am thinking it right as a math optimization exercise, the idea would be to start with 0 dots on the Asset skills, and spend at least 4 merit dots to get the 3rd and 4th abilities. 3rd gives you a third Asset skill and two specialties (which should be on hold until you buy the skill dots) and 4th gives you a beat every time you purchase a dot on the Asset skills.<br /> <br /> Does my analysis make sense? Besides the ST disallowing it, is there any reason why this shouldn't work as described?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mechanically speaking, there is no restriction. But the merit assumes this is how your character earns their keep, so I would want them to have at least two dots in both asset skills (which normally equates to professional level in the core book) to justify it, even if they don't have specialties. If the player wanted to get the best cost-benefit, I think picking up the third asset skill from scratch could make for a good balance between roleplay and mechanical benefit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-14T18:14:48-07:00","id":1537376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1537336#post1537336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4 dice pool for ([attribute 5] - 1 unskilled) should work well enough for some jobs.<br /> <br /> Especially a player character who can spend willpower on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not so much what I meant.<br /> <br /> In the corporate world, some people just get there despite incompetence. It's not by having peak human talent, no, they can effectively have a Chance Die to do their job. They game the system, their contacts and their power.<br /> <br /> Ever heard of the manager who have subordinates do every single aspect of their work, but is close friends to their superiors? Even a mechanic could, <b>in an extreme case</b>, let others do their work and take the credit.<br /> <br /> Of course, most professionals aren't those types, and most of those types would still have at least 1 dot in each skill. But the extreme cases do exist, and PCs are extreme cases by definition.<br /> <br /> All in all, &quot;gaming&quot; Professional Training is actually a lot of effort for very dubious return, as the whole thing is predicated on devoting a lot of XP to two skills, so I don't see the need to enforce a minimum as long as the player has it very clear what this entails for their life as a professional.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-15T20:54:20-07:00","id":1537459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1537338#post1537338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> so someone as talented and strong/smart/whatever as to be at PEAK human condition, so talented beyond belief, goes down a career path where they have 0 skills, and manage to stay on that career path long enough to build up Professional Training to 4 dots, but yet fail to pick up a single dot of relevant skills?<br /> <br /> I've seen some blatant min-maxing from my players, and it's fine, but c'mon, at least keep the characters story arc believable alongside their traits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Peak human ability but too lazy to learn who just improvises their way through life getting by on their natural talent.<br /> <br /> Yeah, that doesn't remind me of anyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-16T01:44:23-07:00","id":1537473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1537459#post1537459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Peak human ability but too lazy to learn who just improvises their way through life getting by on their natural talent.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that maybe justifies a 3 rather than a 2 in an attribute, not 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-17T03:48:23-07:00","id":1537553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1537459#post1537459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Peak human ability but too lazy to learn who just improvises their way through life getting by on their natural talent.<br /> <br /> Yeah, that doesn't remind me of anyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Getting by does not sound &quot;Professional training 4&quot;, with the contacts in the field and the like.<br /> <br /> And even what monteparmas is describing - still sounds like someone with social skills.<br /> <br /> So maybe their professional training is &quot;Mechanic&quot;, but they take one of their Asset skills to be &quot;Socialize&quot;, or fuck &quot;Socialize and Persuasion&quot;, for their first two asset skills, and Crafts as their third, meaning, they are in mechanics field, but really, their &quot;job&quot; skills are the social ones - that's what they use on the day to day, to be so liked by their colleagues to keep the job and at some point, they're starting to pick up the relevant skill, because they're in the field and all these friends will <i>happily</i> teach them. Or NOT! The last skill could be Subterfuge to keep on lying about how they do all the necessary things around here, while others are picking up the slack.<br /> <br /> Context matters. And that's what I'd expect from a character sheet with a backstory - for their traits to make sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":294,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","user":"Griautis","date":". 06-17-2024, 06:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-17T16:40:47-07:00","id":1537590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1537553#post1537553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Getting by does not sound &quot;Professional training 4&quot;, with the contacts in the field and the like.<br /> <br /> And even what monteparmas is describing - still sounds like someone with social skills.<br /> <br /> So maybe their professional training is &quot;Mechanic&quot;, but they take one of their Asset skills to be &quot;Socialize&quot;, or fuck &quot;Socialize and Persuasion&quot;, for their first two asset skills, and Crafts as their third, meaning, they are in mechanics field, but really, their &quot;job&quot; skills are the social ones - that's what they use on the day to day, to be so liked by their colleagues to keep the job and at some point, they're starting to pick up the relevant skill, because they're in the field and all these friends will <i>happily</i> teach them. Or NOT! The last skill could be Subterfuge to keep on lying about how they do all the necessary things around here, while others are picking up the slack.<br /> <br /> Context matters. And that's what I'd expect from a character sheet with a backstory - for their traits to make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>My first Storyteller revised the entire character sheet asking questions about how each and every dot was there. And he promptly forced changes when he thought something didn't made sense, regardless if it made for the player. Making a new character with him was an arduous task, full of anxiety and frustration, and the end result wasn't all that rewarding, it was his vision of the character, not ours.<br /> <br /> This is my context. I don't like this kind of intrusion on the player's character. It rubs me in all the wrong ways.<br /> <br /> As a storyteller I do ask questions about the sheet, but I don't want it to make sense to me, I want it to tell a story, the player will enjoy. Without pressure, this is just a game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-20T09:18:46-07:00","id":1537710,"title":"","content":"When it comes to Touchstones in general, could a character have a the unborn baby be a Touchstone while the one carrying the bag isn't. Also, if a person is pregnant with multiples, could a character have one baby be a Touchstone while the other isn't? Some examples of how this could work:<br /> <br /> A sexist husband who views his wife as a baby machine only carrying about his unborn child because it's his first son.<br /> <br /> A person who hates their ex-spouse but loves their unborn child.<br /> <br /> A person paying someone to act as a surrogate who views the surrogate as a business partner.\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-20T15:32:50-07:00","id":1537728,"title":"","content":"Those are all things to ask your table if they are comfortable with. There's no RAW.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-20T17:29:58-07:00","id":1537731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1537710#post1537710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When it comes to Touchstones in general, could a character have a the unborn baby be a Touchstone while the one carrying the bag isn't. Also, if a person is pregnant with multiples, could a character have one baby be a Touchstone while the other isn't? Some examples of how this could work:<br /> <br /> A sexist husband who views his wife as a baby machine only carrying about his unborn child because it's his first son.<br /> <br /> A person who hates their ex-spouse but loves their unborn child.<br /> <br /> A person paying someone to act as a surrogate who views the surrogate as a business partner.\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>It certainly can, which doesn't mean it should.<br /> <br /> This really is something to discuss with the group, to be sure that everyone is ok with that. If even one person at the table has reservations about this, it's better to look for another Touchstone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-20T18:47:47-07:00","id":1537744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1537710#post1537710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When it comes to Touchstones in general, could a character have a the unborn baby be a Touchstone while the one carrying the bag isn't. Also, if a person is pregnant with multiples, could a character have one baby be a Touchstone while the other isn't?</div> </div> </div> </div>As previously discussed, most Touchstone systems are built under the assumption that the Touchstone is a character, which an unborn child obviously is not.<br /> <br /> A baby in utero is not going to test a vampire's Requiem in any way that would not be equally or better represented by the person carrying the child, who is presumably not a stranger.<br /> <br /> An unborn child does not have any manner of two-way relationship that a werewolf can draw upon to anchor their Harmony, though the potential it represents could ostensibly be used in the same fashion as more abstract Touchstones like The Locus or The Religion.<br /> <br /> A kid in the womb is not going to teach a changeling how to trust again, and spending a scene &quot;meaningfully interacting with&quot; it as a distinct entity from the person it's gestating in is going to be functionally impossible or at least an exceedingly hard sell for your table.<br /> <br /> A Synergy Touchstone represents a promise, whether relating to your Burden or your Remembrance, and while some of those theoretically have room to apply to an unborn baby, most of them are once again more reasonably tied to characters who are characters who can be engaged with in the story at the time the relationship is tagged.<br /> <br /> If you are a monster hunter, an unborn baby is definitionally not someone you will feel safe around who can help keep you grounded, much less serve as someone you can open up to or trust with your life in a way that wouldn't be better handled by the carrying parent.<br /> <br /> Children in the womb are not characters and thus do not have Virtues or Vices and thus are completely and utterly outside the mechanical scope of Arisen Touchstones, end of story.<br /> <br /> You asked a variant of this question with relation to deviant Touchstones <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1510923#post1510923\">a year ago</a>.<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, the things Touchstones represent exist to drive social/emotional interactions with a specific part of the setting, most commonly and beneficially a character, and an unborn child itself typically contributes constructively to that tool about as well as a donor organ and with the same baked-in question about the player's choice of focuses when there's a different part of the setting wrapped around it that is more conversant or at least better able to be engaged with the systems meant for dealing with people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-22T04:17:25-07:00","id":1537795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1537731#post1537731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This really is something to discuss with the group, to be sure that everyone is ok with that. If even one person at the table has reservations about this, it's better to look for another Touchstone.</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt he has a group, all his posts are about trying to be as edgy as possible and cover things from attempting to get away with cannibalism to this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-08T10:00:08-07:00","id":1538240,"title":"","content":"Today I was trying to understand and translate to spanish the Investigation system and I <i>think</i> I understand it, but I have a simple question:<br /> <br /> How you, as a GM, narrate a Clue?<br /> <br /> Like, I can, without major problems, narrate everything until the character enters in the governor computer and rolls Wits+Computers to look for juicy blackmail. They succed and let's say he wins a Clue with 2 Elements<br /> <br /> How I narrate that in a way that isn't a hard clue (in the sense that the clue can't solve the case by itself) but still feels <i>like a Clue</i>?<br /> <br /> How I narrate he expending Elements to boost another roll to find clues through tailing the governor that he does the next session?<br /> <br /> How I narrate that expending of Elements making, latter, that he solves the investigation &quot;with complications&quot;?<br /> <br /> How these narration change if he win a Clue with 5 Elements with Merits?<br /> <br /> Maybe is the way we play, but I really struggle imagining how to <i>narrate</i> the acquisition and use of Clues when they are mostly abstract.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27384,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27384-altidiya","user":"altidiya","date":".  Adding the 5 Elements question 07-08-2024, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27384-altidiya","name":"altidiya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-08T15:37:53-07:00","id":1538259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>altidiya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1538240#post1538240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, I can, without major problems, narrate everything until the character enters in the governor computer and rolls Wits+Computers to look for juicy blackmail. They succed and let's say he wins a Clue with 2 Elements</div> </div> </div> </div>Following along with the example\u2026<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How I narrate that in a way that isn't a hard clue (in the sense that the clue can't solve the case by itself) but still feels <i>like a Clue</i>? </div> </div> </div>Present information that is suspicious but not conclusive, like a pattern of purchases or visits to a location outside of his expected routine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How I narrate he expending Elements to boost another roll to find clues through tailing the governor that he does the next session? </div> </div> </div>Depends what the elements are, but maybe they use the element they got from their Art History Specialty to identify that all those different museum visits were during limited-time exhibits to figure out where he's likely to be going.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How I narrate that expending of Elements making, latter, that he solves the investigation &quot;with complications&quot;? </div> </div> </div>Multiple elements of a Clue are still part of the same Clue (added through expertise and/or exceptional luck), and solving the investigation with complications happens when there's a shortfall of the required number of Clues. Maybe the player declares that the governor is in on an artifact-smuggling ring and without extra information their blackmail attempts will trip over the paranoid precautions of his sorcerous partner in crime. Maybe the governor's been paying enough attention to send the police after them. Maybe he's simply prepared enough that their attempt at blackmail won't stick well enough to compel him to do anything on its own.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How these narration change if he win a Clue with 5 Elements with Merits? </div> </div> </div>Same deal as above; it doesn't matter that one of the Clues has five elements if you need more than one Clue to cleanly solve the investigation. Five elements from a single Clue is very useful for an investigator who doesn't have a lot of Investigation and/or Clues to work with, but they won't complete the picture in a way that narratively blocks a plot twist from coming up behind you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe is the way we play, but I really struggle imagining how to <i>narrate</i> the acquisition and use of Clues when they are mostly abstract. </div> </div> </div>The gist of it is that in an investigation the characters are collecting Clues to assemble to find the truth; elements and tags allow the Clues they discover to help them, whether with the investigation or peripherally related tasks, and to make it so that the characters can't conclusively put the picture together without more information and/or without dispelling false leads. You can jump to the end with a single complete Clue at any time, provided you're willing to accept that the outcome includes you having overlooked something vital or failed to prepare for the aftermath.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-08T17:09:14-07:00","id":1538262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1538259#post1538259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Following along with the example\u2026<br /> <br /> Same deal as above; it doesn't matter that one of the Clues has five elements if you need more than one Clue to cleanly solve the investigation. Five elements from a single Clue is very useful for an investigator who doesn't have a lot of Investigation and/or Clues to work with, but they won't complete the picture in a way that narratively blocks a plot twist from coming up behind you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I was under the idea that Clue without Elements are <i>what</i> creates the complication. In the sense that if I have a 5 Clue Mystery and I have 5 Clues, but only 3 Elements between them, I can solve the case with 2 Complications. So &quot;Elementless&quot; Clues were mostly useless withuot a Clue with more Elements.<br /> <br /> But then, you can solve the case with one single Clue if you are up to take the Complications?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27384-altidiya","name":"altidiya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-08T18:31:11-07:00","id":1538266,"title":"","content":"What magic could protect Vampire from Sunlight or at least taking less damage from the sun?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-08T19:28:13-07:00","id":1538275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>altidiya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1538262#post1538262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I was under the idea that Clue without Elements are <i>what</i> creates the complication. In the sense that if I have a 5 Clue Mystery and I have 5 Clues, but only 3 Elements between them, I can solve the case with 2 Complications. So &quot;Elementless&quot; Clues were mostly useless withuot a Clue with more Elements.<br /> <br /> But then, you can solve the case with one single Clue if you are up to take the Complications?</div> </div> </div> </div>Every Clue has at least one element, which can be spent on rolls relating to those elements for bonus dice. Incomplete Clues garnered from a failed roll can't be used to ultimately solve the case and can only help you with rolls to find more Clues, while tainted Clues from a dramatic failure sabotage future investigation rolls and likewise don't count toward the total needed for the investigation until you spend the tainted element(s) to penalize a roll and make the Clue work like a normal Clue.<br /> <br /> As long as you have at least one Clue that isn't tainted, you can try to put together the answer, but the type of complications a shortfall produces are such that you're really taking your chances inviting more than one or two of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-09T05:33:35-07:00","id":1538293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1538266#post1538266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What magic could protect Vampire from Sunlight or at least taking less damage from the sun?</div> </div> </div> </div>Simplest one I can think of is a mage using a Shielding of Forces on them. Since people aren't assumed to burn in the sunlight, it wouldn't be at risk of Disbelief.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-09T05:37:00-07:00","id":1538294,"title":"","content":"Anything else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-09T14:36:43-07:00","id":1538326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1538294#post1538294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anything else?</div> </div> </div> </div>Matter could be used to build &quot;sunproof&quot; clothes<br /> <br /> Space can create a distorted field where light bends without hitting the vampire, but it would be blind for the duration<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-09T14:59:12-07:00","id":1538328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1538326#post1538326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Matter could be used to build &quot;sunproof&quot; clothes<br /> <br /> Space can create a distorted field where light bends without hitting the vampire, but it would be blind for the duration<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You don't need &quot;sunproof&quot; clothes in 2nd Edition. As long as you cover the entire body, any clothes seem to work.<br /> <br /> Matter would be more interesting at treating sunglasses, as the eyes remain potentially vulnerable.<br /> <br /> How much protection of any kind prevents a vampire from burning ultimately depends on the ST, although Secrets of the Covenants has at least one example that it shouldn't be too big of a concern.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day it's a matter of what's best for your story, there's no real balance issue behind it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-10T06:43:37-07:00","id":1538356,"title":"","content":"Why does Hunter have touchstone but non-hunter Mortal don't? Can a non-hunter Mortal have touchstone with Touchstone merit from Hunter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-10T07:45:27-07:00","id":1538358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1538356#post1538356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why does Hunter have touchstone but non-hunter Mortal don't? Can a non-hunter Mortal have touchstone with Touchstone merit from Hunter?</div> </div> </div> </div>Touchstones are really just there to encourage roleplaying a connection to a normal person, since blue book mortals are normal people they don't really need one. As to wether or not they can take the touchstone merit, that's entirely storyteller dependent, some may be fine with it while others may not want to deal with the mechanics or may just not want to have stuff from other books. <br /> <br /> You're always allowed to have NPCs your character cares about though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-10T11:56:26-07:00","id":1538382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1538356#post1538356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why does Hunter have touchstone but non-hunter Mortal don't? Can a non-hunter Mortal have touchstone with Touchstone merit from Hunter?</div> </div> </div> </div>Notably there's very little that having a Touchstone would actually <i>do</i> for a normal mortal under the conventional models; it could add dice bonuses to breaking point rolls, sure, but vanilla Integrity doesn't really differentiate all that much at different levels, so any additional benefits would depend heavily on what the purpose of adding Touchstones to your game is \u2014 you might take cues from Geist and Deviant and have Touchstones relate to specific pursuits, whether those pursuits are other Anchors or Aspirations, but then you have to define what that category of pursuit is and why having higher Integrity and/or maintaining a related Touchstone helps with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-10T13:50:56-07:00","id":1538386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1538356#post1538356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why does Hunter have touchstone but non-hunter Mortal don't? Can a non-hunter Mortal have touchstone with Touchstone merit from Hunter?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hunter's Integrity trait, despite the name, is a very different trait that's setting out to do something different from what the non-hunter Integrity trait does.<br /> <br /> Characters use Touchstones to anchor themselves and their experiences in their human (or humanlike) life. Vampires anchor themselves in attachments to the living. Werewolves anchor themselves against losing too much of their human perspective or their primal spirit. Changelings anchor themselves to points of stability amid mad faerie dreams. Hunters anchor themselves to a life that's more than just keeping Vigil, without which their Vigil loses meaning and perspective.<br /> <br /> Non-hunter mortals would anchor themselves to... what? They don't intrinsically have two feet in different worlds. Losing Integrity represents shock, trauma, and a loss of a stable mental attitude. If you were to make Touchstones for ordinary Integrity, one would imagine this would be what they would represent: islands of comfort and rocks of certainty in a turbulent world, sources of support that can be counted on. Not just your <i>closest</i> relationships, but specifically your most <i>reassuring</i> ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-11T05:57:13-07:00","id":1538423,"title":"","content":"What is the purpose of the circle Health box and Willpower?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-11T06:24:17-07:00","id":1538425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1538423#post1538423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the purpose of the circle Health box and Willpower?</div> </div> </div> </div>Circles are permanent, squares are temporary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-12T00:19:35-07:00","id":1538467,"title":"","content":"How does a shared merit work when there're more than 5 players? Or like when the shared merit have only 2 dot like Telepathic Bound?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-12T05:20:21-07:00","id":1538471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1538467#post1538467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does a shared merit work when there're more than 5 players? Or like when the shared merit have only 2 dot like Telepathic Bound?</div> </div> </div> </div>Characters must spend at least one dot to buy in to a pooled Merit, even if that dot doesn't do anything. Notably the books consistently describe the ideal play group size as 2-5 players including the Storyteller.<br /> <br /> Telepathic Bond is not a shared Merit; everyone in the group purchases it separately at its listed cost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-12T05:56:02-07:00","id":1538472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1538471#post1538471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Characters must spend at least one dot to buy in to a pooled Merit, even if that dot doesn't do anything. Notably the books consistently describe the ideal play group size as 2-5 players including the Storyteller.<br /> <br /> Telepathic Bond is not a shared Merit; everyone in the group purchases it separately at its listed cost.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, you could pooled in a six dot, even if it doesn't actually do anything?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-12T05:57:26-07:00","id":1538473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1538472#post1538472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, you could pooled in a six dot, even if it doesn't actually do anything?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's correct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T08:48:50-07:00","id":1538758,"title":"","content":"I'm a little confused about Touchstones with Hunter: the Vigil 2e, do touchstones get slotted to specific Integrity values? What happens if you drop below that Integrity level? I'm sure it says it somewhere but I apparently keep missing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25650-jacook03","name":"Jacook03","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25650_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T11:27:39-07:00","id":1538771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacook03</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1538758#post1538758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a little confused about Touchstones with Hunter: the Vigil 2e, do touchstones get slotted to specific Integrity values? What happens if you drop below that Integrity level? I'm sure it says it somewhere but I apparently keep missing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chapter 3, under Touchstones: Systems.<br /> You attach your first Touchstone to Integrity 6, and if you have multiple Touchstones, further Touchstones attach at 5, 4, 3, 2, 1. The Touchstone is considered &quot;attached&quot; when your Integrity equals or exceeds the rating it's attached to, and &quot;unattached&quot; if you drop below. An unattached Touchstone isn't outright lost, and reattaches the moment you meet its Integrity level again.<br /> <br /> You only gain Willpower from defending attached Touchstones and only gain bonuses to resist breaking points from attached Touchstones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T12:18:57-07:00","id":1538775,"title":"","content":"Much appreciated. I know I read that section several times but just seems to have missed it every time. Pg. 72, right side the page.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25650-jacook03","name":"Jacook03","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25650_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-28T01:40:17-07:00","id":1539413,"title":"","content":"If you have 4 dot in Resource and 3 dot in Plutomancy Resource, do you gain 6 Plutomancy point?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-30T00:05:06-07:00","id":1539519,"title":"","content":"Does Hunter with Vector count as Sleepwalker?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-31T10:45:51-07:00","id":1539595,"title":"","content":"Could you use Peacemaker (from Hurt Locker) to intervene between two other characters/groups who both want to fight each other? Any ideas about how that should work, if so?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-31T15:04:56-07:00","id":1539606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1539595#post1539595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you use Peacemaker (from Hurt Locker) to intervene between two other characters/groups who both want to fight each other? Any ideas about how that should work, if so?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say yes. As for ideas - if both groups are seeking violent outcome, then you'd have to succeed with the use of this merit against both groups. Note, given that the merit only _protects_ you, from violence while it's in effect ,the groups might start throwing punches as you're trying to talk them out of it. Depending on who the involved groups are, successful damage, might add or remove doors from your attempts. <br /> <br /> Once you open all the doors on both sides (and thusm both sides are seeking non-violent solution), they cease fighting. <br /> <br /> If only one side is violently inclined and another is just defending or some such then you just use the merit against the violently inclined group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-04T18:53:56-07:00","id":1539812,"title":"","content":"In Parkour Cat Leap, it said that you can add Parkour rating to the threshold of damage that can be removed through this roll. But what does this mean? Since there is no threshold for the amount of damage that you can remove from falling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-04T21:19:44-07:00","id":1539822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1539812#post1539812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Parkour Cat Leap, it said that you can add Parkour rating to the threshold of damage that can be removed through this roll. But what does this mean? Since there is no threshold for the amount of damage that you can remove from falling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I know this! It's a vestigial rule from when Parkour was a part of the GMC rules update. It's actually referencing the falling rules in the <i>1e core rulebook</i>, which never made the jump to any of the 2e rules [that I am aware of]:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>World of Darkness Core Rulebook, p. 179</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Storyteller may allow your character to try to break his fall by some means, perhaps by grabbing for awnings or twisting to strike soil rather than concrete. A single Dexterity + Athletics roll may be called for], with each success gained diminishing damage taken. <b>There may be a limit to how much damage can be shaved, though - say, three.</b> There's only so much that desperate flailing and grabbing can do when someone falls from a significant height. Efforts to slow one's fall are usually useless at terminal velocity.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a little silly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Posting gives me anxiety, but I'm still happy to be here</i><br /> Habitual Lurker, Vengrel Liker, Acolyte Apologist, She/Her","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25955-somethingfishy","name":"SomethingFishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25955_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T03:22:12-07:00","id":1539837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1539812#post1539812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Parkour Cat Leap, it said that you can add Parkour rating to the threshold of damage that can be removed through this roll. But what does this mean? Since there is no threshold for the amount of damage that you can remove from falling.</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;threshold&quot; is whatever the Storyteller thinks it should be. In 1e, 3 was <i>recommended</i>. The text is the same in some versions of the falling rules now, only without the number. Falling is almost always in action time, so I'd say just always use 3 as the threshold and keep moving.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Didn't see your post until I'd written this, SomethingFishy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28549,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","user":"Sikander","date":". 08-05-2024, 06:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T03:55:42-07:00","id":1539838,"title":"","content":"This would mean that with maximum Parkour, you could reduce falling damage by <i>eight</i>. The likelihood of rolling seven successes, plus your automatic one from Cat Leap, is vanishingly small - but I guess it's nice to know that if you did, you could use them all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T16:45:23-07:00","id":1539896,"title":"","content":"I'd give the Parkour 2-having player the single reduction in falling damage regardless, other than in the case of terminal velocity - someone with Parkour knows how to land to minimize falling damage. I'd only let them roll for more in circumstances where they could reasonably grab something or bounce off a wall to minimize final impact. This is not quite RAW, but I'd do it.<br /> Also, I think three successes is just good. It's the expected outcome of an unmodified action by a Maximallly Capable Human (TM). It's Exceptional Success if some effect gives you easier Exceptional Success. I think it just makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28549,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","user":"Sikander","date":". 08-05-2024, 08:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T19:41:01-07:00","id":1539910,"title":"","content":"Are there rule to create animal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T20:17:33-07:00","id":1539913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1539910#post1539910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there rule to create animal?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a list of animal stats in <a href=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wild-at-heart/\" target=\"_blank\">this blog post</a> linked in one of the pinned posts on this board, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/480383/The-Clades-Companion\" target=\"_blank\">The Clades Companion</a> for Deviant: the Renegades has additional statblocks and general guidance on how to create statblocks for other animals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-10T15:34:31-07:00","id":1540148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1538356#post1538356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why does Hunter have touchstone but non-hunter Mortal don't? Can a non-hunter Mortal have touchstone with Touchstone merit from Hunter?</div> </div> </div> </div>The really interesting question here is &quot;At what point does a blue-book mortal <i>become</i> a hunter, and should the process be modeled mechanically in some way?&quot; I have an answer to that, but it's based in a homebrew Conviction stat that I have added. Does anyone else have an answer? If so, what is it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-10T15:51:30-07:00","id":1540149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1539913#post1539913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a list of animal stats in <a href=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wild-at-heart/\" target=\"_blank\">this blog post</a> linked in one of the pinned posts on this board, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/480383/The-Clades-Companion\" target=\"_blank\">The Clades Companion</a> for Deviant: the Renegades has additional statblocks and general guidance on how to create statblocks for other animals.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Clades Companion also has a &quot;scar repressor&quot; equipment that came at a time when I was independently working up something I was calling a &quot;bane suit,&quot; mainly for changelings. I don't play Deviant, but there's stuff in there to mine even if you don't either. Surveillance rolls could give elder vampires a reason, beyond mere dickishness/risk aversion, to palm off the actual work on the young. And everyone who does conspiratorial stuff could probably benefit from conspiracy maps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28549,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","user":"Sikander","date":". 08-11-2024, 07:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-15T18:16:51-07:00","id":1540487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1540148#post1540148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The really interesting question here is &quot;At what point does a blue-book mortal <i>become</i> a hunter, and should the process be modeled mechanically in some way?&quot; I have an answer to that, but it's based in a homebrew Conviction stat that I have added. Does anyone else have an answer? If so, what is it?</div> </div> </div> </div>My personal answer is that no, it should not be modelled mechanically. It happens when you dedicate an ongoing part of your life to the Vigil. When exactly to apply the distinction is a judgment call and should be salted to taste based on what feels dramatically appropriate for the chronicle in question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-20T09:42:07-07:00","id":1540784,"title":"","content":"If a supernatural being belongs to a Mystery Cult that grants its members supernatural merits, can the creature gains those merits?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-20T09:59:07-07:00","id":1540786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1540784#post1540784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a supernatural being belongs to a Mystery Cult that grants its members supernatural merits, can the creature gains those merits?</div> </div> </div> </div>They would spend those Merit dots on Merits they are able to take normally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-22T05:04:26-07:00","id":1540884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1540487#post1540487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My personal answer is that no, it should not be modelled mechanically. It happens when you dedicate an ongoing part of your life to the Vigil. When exactly to apply the distinction is a judgment call and should be salted to taste based on what feels dramatically appropriate for the chronicle in question.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite what I meant. Of course taking up the Vigil is a character decision - but if that decision is made in play rather than prelude, does anyone &quot;phase in&quot; the altered Hunter Integrity rules? Do other people make new Hunters pay Experience for their first Touchstone, or just hand it out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-22T06:31:43-07:00","id":1540887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1540884#post1540884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not quite what I meant. Of course taking up the Vigil is a character decision - but if that decision is made in play rather than prelude, does anyone &quot;phase in&quot; the altered Hunter Integrity rules? Do other people make new Hunters pay Experience for their first Touchstone, or just hand it out?</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't matter what you do, so long as you're consistent for your whole group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-22T07:38:24-07:00","id":1540888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1540784#post1540784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a supernatural being belongs to a Mystery Cult that grants its members supernatural merits, can the creature gains those merits?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Hurt Locker </i>has a tab on page 71 about granting these merits to major splats. They were designed to be used by minor templates, but can be given to major splats, so long as the GM is fine with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-10T00:20:48-07:00","id":1541837,"title":"","content":"In Contagion Chronicle for Godhead Vector &quot;but at the end of your time as the Godhead, all lethal and bashing damage is healed.&quot; Does this happen before or after the lethal damage have been turn into aggravated damage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-10T06:36:25-07:00","id":1541857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1541837#post1541837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Contagion Chronicle for Godhead Vector &quot;but at the end of your time as the Godhead, all lethal and bashing damage is healed.&quot; Does this happen before or after the lethal damage have been turn into aggravated damage?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it matters because the damage you take from the Godhead Vector &quot;cannot be healed in any way&quot; so the healing doesn't trump the cannot be healed. In general though, I would default to whichever answer was more favorable to the Hunter if anything ever did come up from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-10T06:51:14-07:00","id":1541858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div cla