 like how Vampire, Werewolf, and Beast Edge add Smell to the Sight and Hearing Vector.</div> </div> </div> </div>So... did you only ask the question in order to get told what you wanted to hear? Because you obviously weren't asking the question to discover the answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-10T07:58:15-07:00","id":1541865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1541864#post1541864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So... did you only ask the question in order to get told what you wanted to hear? Because you obviously weren't asking the question to discover the answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I ask the question just to be sure my interpertation of the rule was correct, I know that Edge trump the rule of the Vector as written, but I don't know if the Hunter Godhead Edge is suppose to heal the Lethal Damage before they become Aggravated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-10T07:59:37-07:00","id":1541866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1541865#post1541865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, I ask the question just to be sure my interpertation of the rule was correct, I know that Edge trump the rule of the Vector as written, but I don't know if the Hunter Godhead Edge is suppose to heal the Lethal Damage before they become Aggravated.</div> </div> </div> </div>And you got told &quot;no, the unhealable damage doesn't just get healed&quot; and then you proceeded to argue. It really seems like you only asked the question in order to get told what you wanted to be told.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-10T08:07:10-07:00","id":1541867,"title":"","content":"Well, because your answer doesn't make sense because if your answer is true, then the Edge become useless if you can't heal from the lethal damage you took from being a Godhead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-10T09:44:53-07:00","id":1541872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1541867#post1541867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, because your answer doesn't make sense because if your answer is true, then the Edge become useless if you can't heal from the lethal damage you took from being a Godhead.</div> </div> </div> </div>First off, why ask the question if only one option makes sense? Second, what do you think is happening around the PC at the time when they activate the massively powerful combat ability? Maybe something that could cause them to take damage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-10T12:41:07-07:00","id":1541880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1541872#post1541872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First off, why ask the question if only one option makes sense? Second, what do you think is happening around the PC at the time when they activate the massively powerful combat ability? Maybe something that could cause them to take damage?</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the effects of Godhead is immunity to any Health damage other than the per-turn toll of the power itself.<br /> <br /> Presumably the &quot;cannot be healed in any way&quot; part of that damage is a check against regeneration or other self-healing being used to functionally extend the duration of the power without spending Willpower.<br /> <br /> Given that hunters don't get any other benefits from Godhead and the Vector is metered in how frequently it can be used by the Condition it leaves behind (we will, for sanity's sake, ignore the wording of the rules that indicates you can only use it once no matter what as an obvious error), I don't think much breaks in allowing the lethal damage that functions as a kill timer to be healed as soon as you stop benefiting from the Vector, given the directly comparable benefits of going loud for demons (or, for that matter, vampires getting +2 BP and full Vitae or changeling getting five Hedgespinning successes that can be used even outside the Hedge).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-10T14:03:02-07:00","id":1541884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1541880#post1541880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the effects of Godhead is immunity to any Health damage other than the per-turn toll of the power itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it doesn't heal damage sustained before hand.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Presumably the &quot;cannot be healed in any way&quot; part of that damage is a check against regeneration or other self-healing being used to functionally extend the duration of the power without spending Willpower. </div> </div> </div>You can guess at the intent, and you make a fair case, but it's still not what the rules say. The rules say the lethal damage can't be healed and the hunter is explicitly healing damage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Given that hunters don't get any other benefits from Godhead </div> </div> </div>Huh? Hunters gain tons of benefits, same as everyone else. There's a reason this is a level 5 power. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and the Vector is metered in how frequently it can be used by the Condition it leaves behind (we will, for sanity's sake, ignore the wording of the rules that indicates you can only use it once no matter what as an obvious error), I don't think much breaks in allowing the lethal damage that functions as a kill timer to be healed as soon as you stop benefiting from the Vector, </div> </div> </div>That's a reasonable house rule but we weren't asked for a house rule. I'm only saying that the rules as written say the damage cannot be healed and the hunter edge is explicitly healing. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> given the directly comparable benefits of going loud for demons (or, for that matter, vampires getting +2 BP and full Vitae or changeling getting five Hedgespinning successes that can be used even outside the Hedge). </div> </div> </div>Edges vary wildly. I'm not sure my interpretation of the rules makes the Hunter edge worse than the Sin Eater edge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-10T16:53:45-07:00","id":1541894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1541884#post1541884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm only saying that the rules as written say the damage cannot be healed and the hunter edge is explicitly healing.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you acknowledge that Hunter edge does heal Lethal damage, but not the Lethal damage you get from Godhead? So what damage does the Edge heal if not for the Lethal damage that we get from Godhead?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-10T17:43:27-07:00","id":1541899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1541837#post1541837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Contagion Chronicle for Godhead Vector &quot;but at the end of your time as the Godhead, all lethal and bashing damage is healed.&quot; Does this happen before or after the lethal damage have been turn into aggravated damage?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you take enough Lethal damage it rolls up into Aggravated immediately. Unless a power eliminates damage during the process of application, which is quite rare and not what's happening here, you'll never &quot;heal before it turns into Agg&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-10T18:58:23-07:00","id":1541907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1541884#post1541884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can guess at the intent, and you make a fair case, but it's still not what the rules say. The rules say the lethal damage can't be healed and the hunter is explicitly healing damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>The rules also say that the power can only be used after the longer of two lengths of time passes and provides one of those lengths of time as the entire game. This is an occasion where appealing to the exact letter of the text is not a useful approach.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Huh? Hunters gain tons of benefits, same as everyone else. There's a reason this is a level 5 power. </div> </div> </div>ShadowCat, I know you are smart enough to understand from context that &quot;healing damage after the power ends is the only benefit hunters get from Godhead&quot; comes with an unstated &quot;aside from everything the base Vector gives&quot; when I am talking about the relative benefits of their Edge compared to those afforded to other splats.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's a reasonable house rule but we weren't asked for a house rule. I'm only saying that the rules as written say the damage cannot be healed and the hunter edge is explicitly healing. </div> </div> </div>For a power that explicitly makes you immune to damage and counts its duration in terms of inflicting damage on you each turn that you don't buy off with Willpower expenditure. If a direct reading makes the power not make sense then interpretation is a reasonable next step.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Edges vary wildly. I'm not sure my interpretation of the rules makes the Hunter edge worse than the Sin Eater edge. </div> </div> </div>The Sin-Eater Edge gives you the ability to identify what Conditions affect people and know their recent dirty secrets, which thematically relates to the vector's illusion-piercing effect.<br /> <br /> If the Hunter Edge can only heal damage marked prior to the activation of the power \u2014 damage that still reduces the effective length of the vector's countdown, since the Edge applies its benefit after the power ends, when the activation of the power takes an instant action and a Willpower and the damage/Willpower surcharge starts applying the turn after the vector is activated \u2014 then it is at its most useful when the full heal is <i>all it will be providing</i>, because needing to have at least two Willpower and/or three unmarked Health left to be able to do anything else is an exceedingly narrow practical use criterion for such a tightly metered power.<br /> <br /> The Hunter Edge applies at the end of your time as the Godhead. Ambiguous sentence structure indicates that the conversion of all the damage you suffered from using the Godhead either happens when the power ends at all or when you run out of Health boxes (and given the immediate description of what happens to characters killed in this fashion, it seems evident that the conversion is intended to kill a character who runs out the clock without the usual several minutes of bleeding out).<br /> <br /> There is a case to be made for voluntarily ending the Godhead keeping the damage it inflicts lethal. There is a legitimate argument to be made that when the power talks about damage not being healable by any means that note exists to prevent the timer from being extended by healing abilities rather than to obviate the purpose of marking a specific damage type. The power has an inbuilt mechanism for preventing immediately healing the damage it does after the end of the power from allowing the character to use it again straight away.<br /> <br /> I've made my case. People can agree with it, come up with their own interpretation, or grapple with the complications of adhering to the strict letter of the text. Godhead is a messily-written power and we're far enough out from the errata collection for Contagion Chronicle that we have to make our peace with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-11T04:55:10-07:00","id":1541921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1541907#post1541907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rules also say that the power can only be used after the longer of two lengths of time passes and provides one of those lengths of time as the entire game. This is an occasion where appealing to the exact letter of the text is not a useful approach.<br /> <br /> ShadowCat, I know you are smart enough to understand from context that &quot;healing damage after the power ends is the only benefit hunters get from Godhead&quot; comes with an unstated &quot;aside from everything the base Vector gives&quot; when I am talking about the relative benefits of their Edge compared to those afforded to other splats.<br /> <br /> For a power that explicitly makes you immune to damage and counts its duration in terms of inflicting damage on you each turn that you don't buy off with Willpower expenditure. If a direct reading makes the power not make sense then interpretation is a reasonable next step.<br /> <br /> The Sin-Eater Edge gives you the ability to identify what Conditions affect people and know their recent dirty secrets, which thematically relates to the vector's illusion-piercing effect.<br /> <br /> If the Hunter Edge can only heal damage marked prior to the activation of the power \u2014 damage that still reduces the effective length of the vector's countdown, since the Edge applies its benefit after the power ends, when the activation of the power takes an instant action and a Willpower and the damage/Willpower surcharge starts applying the turn after the vector is activated \u2014 then it is at its most useful when the full heal is <i>all it will be providing</i>, because needing to have at least two Willpower and/or three unmarked Health left to be able to do anything else is an exceedingly narrow practical use criterion for such a tightly metered power.<br /> <br /> The Hunter Edge applies at the end of your time as the Godhead. Ambiguous sentence structure indicates that the conversion of all the damage you suffered from using the Godhead either happens when the power ends at all or when you run out of Health boxes (and given the immediate description of what happens to characters killed in this fashion, it seems evident that the conversion is intended to kill a character who runs out the clock without the usual several minutes of bleeding out).<br /> <br /> There is a case to be made for voluntarily ending the Godhead keeping the damage it inflicts lethal. There is a legitimate argument to be made that when the power talks about damage not being healable by any means that note exists to prevent the timer from being extended by healing abilities rather than to obviate the purpose of marking a specific damage type. The power has an inbuilt mechanism for preventing immediately healing the damage it does after the end of the power from allowing the character to use it again straight away.<br /> <br /> I've made my case. People can agree with it, come up with their own interpretation, or grapple with the complications of adhering to the strict letter of the text. Godhead is a messily-written power and we're far enough out from the errata collection for Contagion Chronicle that we have to make our peace with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>So when you say something is the only benefit a group gains everyone reading your writing should know you mean &quot;it's the only benefit besides all the other benefits&quot;? <br /> <br /> Also, just because one set of rules is flawed doesn't mean you can't use the rules in another thing. If it did then no ruleset would ever be usable. It's better to treat the individual rules as individual rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-11T05:25:44-07:00","id":1541922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1541921#post1541921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So when you say something is the only benefit a group gains everyone reading your writing should know you mean &quot;it's the only benefit besides all the other benefits&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>When this is from a post that <i>started</i> with describing one of the other benefits and the &quot;only benefit&quot; is described in a paragraph comparing it to the other additional benefits different splats get? Yes, I assume the other participants in the conversation are capable of reading my statements in good faith and with a basic understanding of context.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, just because one set of rules is flawed doesn't mean you can't use the rules in another thing. If it did then no ruleset would ever be usable. It's better to treat the individual rules as individual rules. </div> </div> </div>The question that initiated this discussion was about the order of operations for a pair of effects on a power whose text is less than totally unambiguously worded with regards to how it plays out in practice. Appealing to the text over all else is not a helpful way to proceed, nor is saying that the individual mechanics of those effects are clear useful when the problem is determining how they interact.<br /> <br /> Unless you have something to point to to actually cleanly resolve that interaction, we're stuck with interpretation, and we've both stated our respective interpretations and there's little else to say on this subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-11T06:13:00-07:00","id":1541923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1541922#post1541922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When this is from a post that <i>started</i> with describing one of the other benefits and the &quot;only benefit&quot; is described in a paragraph comparing it to the other additional benefits different splats get? Yes, I assume the other participants in the conversation are capable of reading my statements in good faith and with a basic understanding of context.<br /> <br /> The question that initiated this discussion was about the order of operations for a pair of effects on a power whose text is less than totally unambiguously worded with regards to how it plays out in practice. Appealing to the text over all else is not a helpful way to proceed, nor is saying that the individual mechanics of those effects are clear useful when the problem is determining how they interact.<br /> <br /> Unless you have something to point to to actually cleanly resolve that interaction, we're stuck with interpretation, and we've both stated our respective interpretations and there's little else to say on this subject.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think there's anything ambiguous about damage explicitly stated as not being healable not being healed by the very power that called the damage unhealable, but you do you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-01T20:36:55-07:00","id":1545191,"title":"","content":"Smoking; so, the V:tM: PG has a section on drugs and vampires when drinking the blood, but, doesn't smoking do anything for a vampire, other than make them look cool in CoD?<br /> <br /> Are their rules covering drugs etc.?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-01T21:23:36-07:00","id":1545193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1545191#post1545191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Smoking; so, the V:tM: PG has a section on drugs and vampires when drinking the blood, but, doesn't smoking do anything for a vampire, other than make them look cool in CoD?<br /> <br /> Are their rules covering drugs etc.?</div> </div> </div> </div>Requiem 2e doesn't have specific rules, but Requiem 1e notes that Kindred can get the effects of drugs by either drinking the blood of someone thusly intoxicated or they can spend a Vitae to absorb it directly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":".  Deleted extra word. 11-02-2024, 10:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-10T11:05:30-08:00","id":1545653,"title":"","content":"I am trying to assign dots in skilks backwards: first define what the characters are able or knowledgable about and then putting dots.<br /> <br /> So, if someone would know in game the splats divisions (paths, seemings, auspice, clans) with a general overview of their division powers, and social groupings conflicts (pentacle vs seers, forsaken vs pure, etc), plus knowlege that is equivalent of having read at high level most of the splats core books...<br /> <br /> What level of Occult should this person have? 3, 4, 5 dots? I think 4 is too much for this example because Occult represents also folklore, myths and more beyond <i>&quot;Daeva have emotional manipulation powers, they call it Majesty&quot; </i>or<i> &quot;Mummies serve beings called Judges and have a fivefold soul that they use to fuel their powers&quot;</i><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-10T14:48:39-08:00","id":1545659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1545653#post1545653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am trying to assign dots in skilks backwards: first define what the characters are able or knowledgable about and then putting dots.<br /> <br /> So, if someone would know in game the splats divisions (paths, seemings, auspice, clans) with a general overview of their division powers, and social groupings conflicts (pentacle vs seers, forsaken vs pure, etc), plus knowlege that is equivalent of having read at high level most of the splats core books...<br /> <br /> What level of Occult should this person have? 3, 4, 5 dots? I think 4 is too much for this example because Occult represents also folklore, myths and more beyond <i>&quot;Daeva have emotional manipulation powers, they call it Majesty&quot; </i>or<i> &quot;Mummies serve beings called Judges and have a fivefold soul that they use to fuel their powers&quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Approach the Occult Skill exactly backwards from its standard meaning suggests you've kind of put yourself in a situation where you have to figure out how much of the baseline knowledge they have, because Skills don't represent specific knowledge and the stuff in the splatbooks is largely secret.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-10T17:47:26-08:00","id":1545663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1545659#post1545659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Approach the Occult Skill exactly backwards from its standard meaning suggests you've kind of put yourself in a situation where you have to figure out how much of the baseline knowledge they have, because Skills don't represent specific knowledge and the stuff in the splatbooks is largely secret.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for your reply, so what do you think is the best score given what I have shared?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-10T18:30:36-08:00","id":1545664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1545663#post1545663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for your reply, so what do you think is the best score given what I have shared?</div> </div> </div> </div>However much you feel is appropriate to their knowledge of myth, folklore, urban legend, et cetera, a deficit of which you specifically indicated as a rationale for thinking 4 was too high. I am telling you that what you have shared is not what is used for determining a best score.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-10T18:55:46-08:00","id":1545665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1545664#post1545664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However much you feel is appropriate to their knowledge of myth, folklore, urban legend, et cetera, a deficit of which you specifically indicated as a rationale for thinking 4 was too high. I am telling you that what you have shared is not what is used for determining a best score.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me put it another way, which skill(s) or merit combination best represents then the <b>true </b>knowledge of other splats?<br /> <br /> In Ascension we had Lore (Changing Breeds) or Lore (Vampires) for that specific tidbit of information.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 11-19-2024, 11:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-10T19:19:57-08:00","id":1545666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1545665#post1545665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me put it another way, what skills or merit combination best represents then the true knowledge of other splats?<br /> <br /> In Ascension we had Lore (Changing Breeds) or Lore (Vampires) for that specific tibit of information</div> </div> </div> </div>Encyclopedic Knowledge (Occult), Eye for the Strange, Area of Expertise for a relevant Specialty, and so on.<br /> <br /> Again, the system does not go as granular as &quot;your character has this specific category of knowledge they're not supposed to have,&quot; because if a character knows about Forsaken werewolves it's probably because they're in a game where they're supposed to already know that from their starting context of they found that information in play. Deviant: Shallow Graves introduces a &quot;Transformed Lore&quot; Merit for improving the roll to identify Scars and Variations and make vetted declarations about the powers and weaknesses of a Storyteller character, but deviants are a highly variable template and the Merit only modifies an existing system and lets you exert its narrative control once per story without cost; there isn't a Merit for &quot;you know about deviants&quot; except insofar as having Status in a conspiracy implies you're in the know to some degree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-11T15:37:29-08:00","id":1545713,"title":"","content":"Or to put it another way:<br /> <br /> Being conversant in in-setting lore isn't necessarily something that needs to be enumerated on your sheet. This is less something that you will typically be rolling in-game and more a context around which some rolls will happen. Skill specialties and Merits like Area of Expertise and Interdisciplinary Specialty can help highlight the moments when it's relevant, and Merits like Eye for the Strange and Transformed Lore can optionally provide specific mechanical <i>ways to benefit from</i> your familiarity with the Danse Macabre or the Fallen World. But you're not going to have Lore (Kindred) or Lore (Uratha) where it's a number measuring how much you know.<br /> <br /> You <i>should</i> probably have at least some Occult, though. Occult does include a mix of folklore and supernatural awareness (and in the Chronicles of Darkness a lot of that folklore <i>does</i> turn out to have some kind of application or truth somewhere in the world), and interactions with supernatural beings in the Chronicles of Darkness probably does introduce you to more of that folklore and occultic knowledge, at least in passing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-11T21:22:02-08:00","id":1545725,"title":"","content":"Is there any merit that would help Mortal suck out Essence from Ephemeral being?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-11T22:20:37-08:00","id":1545728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1545725#post1545725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any merit that would help Mortal suck out Essence from Ephemeral being?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing published that doesn't entail changing the character to have an Essence pool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-12T03:41:09-08:00","id":1545736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1545725#post1545725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any merit that would help Mortal suck out Essence from Ephemeral being?</div> </div> </div> </div>It s a bit complex, but:<br /> -a human only pack could buy the Moon s grace merit (from the Pack book)<br /> -with this merit a human can gain Wisdom<br /> -with 2 wisdom dots a Narrator could allow the human to buy the Spiritual blockage merit.<br /> <br /> The Essence drained from the spirit is lost, not gained by the human<br /> <br /> Obviously i am assuming that the spirit/ghost is Materialized or Possessing someone","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24346,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","user":"Neos01","date":". 11-12-2024, 07:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-13T13:07:18-08:00","id":1545810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1545193#post1545193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Requiem 2e doesn't have specific rules, but Requiem 1e notes that Kindred can get the effects of drugs by either drinking the blood of someone thusly intoxicated or they can spend a Vitae to absorb it directly.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Drinking the blood is standard, but, always diluted, as per Masquerade-rules, which are the only solid rules I can go by. So, in other words, a smoking vampire just looks cool?<br /> <br /> Also, if a Forsaken The People started smoking, when they were a teenager, and already changed, wouldn't smoking be a poison and their healing-rates would eliminate any effects of it, almost as quickly as they absorbed it? (Maybe wrong forum); and they are left wondering what people see in smoking?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-13T14:04:28-08:00","id":1545814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1545810#post1545810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Drinking the blood is standard, but, always diluted, as per Masquerade-rules, which are the only solid rules I can go by. So, in other words, a smoking vampire just looks cool?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, if the 1e mechanic carries over, spending Vitae as they would to pass for a living being, which might reasonably be folded into the Blush of Life in general in 2e.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, if a Forsaken The People started smoking, when they were a teenager, and already changed, wouldn't smoking be a poison and their healing-rates would eliminate any effects of it, almost as quickly as they absorbed it? (Maybe wrong forum); and they are left wondering what people see in smoking? </div> </div> </div>The mechanical effects of Primal Urge on drugs are that the werewolf's rating is subtracted from the Toxicity of any poisons, which only comes into play in the case of an overdose. How quickly the recreational effects of drugs fade outside of contexts like Gauru form's supercharged regeneration is presently down to individual tables to decide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-15T15:11:15-07:00","id":1551690,"title":"","content":"Durability? So, if I understand the rules right, does a steel-sword have a chance of breaking if you do more than 3 dots of damage?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-15T17:13:45-07:00","id":1551698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1551690#post1551690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Durability? So, if I understand the rules right, does a steel-sword have a chance of breaking if you do more than 3 dots of damage?</div> </div> </div> </div>Are those not the rules for improvised weapons?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-15T20:32:26-07:00","id":1551705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1551698#post1551698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are those not the rules for improvised weapons?</div> </div> </div> </div>For bronze and silver weapons, actually. Running an Ancients game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-16T09:43:34-07:00","id":1551722,"title":"","content":"Well, it makes sense, as both are far more fragile metals than steel. Silver should probably be even worse than bronze, unless you give them access to silver plating.<br /> <br /> Silver plating exists only since the 18th century, but gold plating has existed for more than 4 or 5 thousand years. While the process for one metal isn't really applicable to the other (not the ancient methods, anyway), in a fictional past this shouldn't be much of a stretch to pretend it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-17T02:25:34-07:00","id":1551734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1551705#post1551705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For bronze and silver weapons, actually. Running an Ancients game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which are where? Like, there are a ton of books this rule could be in.<br /> <br /> I mean, I doubt it either way because swords already have +3 damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-24T19:09:51-07:00","id":1551848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1551734#post1551734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which are where? Like, there are a ton of books this rule could be in.<br /> <br /> I mean, I doubt it either way because swords already have +3 damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>NWoD: Armory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-24T20:16:24-07:00","id":1551851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1551848#post1551848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">NWoD: Armory.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm extremely confused, because the mechanic you mentioned is not included in Armory's writeups on weapon materials and the closest thing to it in that book is a special mechanic for modeling the fragility and awkwardness of using a pocketknife as a weapon (in 1e's systems, a pocketknife is not much better than an improvised weapon, dicepool-wise, and a similar quality is described for large glass bottles in the section on Found and Rigged Weapons).<br /> <br /> Most weapons designed for use as weapons do not break or otherwise suffer damage when wielded with normal human strength.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-25T01:25:29-07:00","id":1551854,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2521_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2521\" data-vbnamecard=\"2521\">Iguazu</a> Okay, I think you have misunderstood the durability mechanic. The lower durability for bronze and silver weapons only comes into play if you actually target the weapon. Simply using the weapon in combat won't do any damage to it (that's why I asked if you were looking at the improvised weapons, because those do suffer damage from use).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-25T16:52:15-07:00","id":1551867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1551854#post1551854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2521_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2521\" data-vbnamecard=\"2521\">Iguazu</a> Okay, I think you have misunderstood the durability mechanic. The lower durability for bronze and silver weapons only comes into play if you actually target the weapon. Simply using the weapon in combat won't do any damage to it (that's why I asked if you were looking at the improvised weapons, because those do suffer damage from use).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I gathered; the WoD-rule book, has rules for specifically targeting the weapon, but, since it was mentioned in <i>Armory</i>, I wanted to make sure there wasn't a special-rule I missed, that the reason we use iron-weapons was that they don't break as easily*. Also, I might, just might, have a D&amp;D bias towards bronze and silver-weapons because there are mechanics in the game that gives them a chance of breaking, per use, not targeted. <br /> <br /> <br /> *Except in ancient Kush; they preferred bronze-weapons and tools because they were easier to repair and worth more than gold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-27T17:31:33-07:00","id":1552675,"title":"","content":"If you join a Mystery Cult and the benefit is a merit or a skill speciality you already have, do you get the Merit dots to spend on things you don't have?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-27T18:42:13-07:00","id":1552678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1552675#post1552675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you join a Mystery Cult and the benefit is a merit or a skill speciality you already have, do you get the Merit dots to spend on things you don't have?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, per the <i>Sanctity of Merits</i> rule (that can be easily applied to Specialties), <b>if they're really the same</b>. Keep in mind that similar, but not quite the same sources of some effects can still count as separate traits in the character sheet. Specialties may be similar without really being the same, even if their uses generally overlap, and that's actually a benefit in the system (as they both apply). Similarly you can have several instances of Safe Place, Allies and a lot of other Merits, some STs even have ways to make distinct instances of Resources relevant. Always see with your ST if this is the case before switching dots around.<br /> <br /> If it really is the case to switch things around, just talk with the ST first to better define what will happen if the Mystery Cult Merit is lost somehow. It's usually easy for the benefits to be taken back by the cult under normal circumstances, but under this change you have to note if the new Merit becomes entangled in the Cult, or if the old, redundant Merits come under attack despite being originally not tied to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-27T19:18:54-07:00","id":1552682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1552675#post1552675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you join a Mystery Cult and the benefit is a merit or a skill speciality you already have, do you get the Merit dots to spend on things you don't have?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, you get the value of the benefit in Merit dots to spend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-10T10:20:08-07:00","id":1553040,"title":"","content":"Apart from Vampires with the Mystery of Zirnitra, can any other kind of supernatural creature somehow purchase supernatural merits?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-10T12:51:34-07:00","id":1553043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1553040#post1553040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apart from Vampires with the Mystery of Zirnitra, can any other kind of supernatural creature somehow purchase supernatural merits?</div> </div> </div> </div>Endless can explicitly purchase Supernatural Merits, as can stigmatics and alchemists; Heralds can purchase Advanced Merits, which are functionally Supernatural Merits expanding on mundane Merits, and ghost eaters can also allocate a number of the Dread Powers they develop to replicate Supernatural Merits on of one-per-dot level.<br /> <br /> There is, of course, also the sidebar in Hurt Locker that essentially says &quot;You're free to remove the humans-only restriction in your games if you want, just be careful about the knock-on effects of doing so,&quot; but that's a bit past the premise of your question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-14T07:41:49-07:00","id":1553166,"title":"","content":"So, I wanted to create a character that is a Baker by trade. What skill would that be represented by? Would it be Craft, Expression or Survival?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-14T07:58:23-07:00","id":1553167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Critian Caceorte</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1553166#post1553166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I wanted to create a character that is a Baker by trade. What skill would that be represented by? Would it be Craft, Expression or Survival?</div> </div> </div> </div>Making food in general isn't consistently covered as a dramatic action requiring a roll, but the distinctions between Crafts and Expression described in the ChroD corebook should serve as a decent guideline \u2014 Expression for artistic stuff, Crafts for &quot;accurate&quot; stuff. Survival is more properly the domain of hunting, foraging, camping, and so on, which has a little overlap but wouldn't be the go-to Skill for someone not attempting to live off the land or survive in the wild.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-14T08:32:59-07:00","id":1553169,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26317\" data-vbnamecard=\"26317\">Critian Caceorte</a> Maybe a dot of Science? Given that baking tends to be about accurate measurement of ingredients and baking times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-14T12:21:00-07:00","id":1553815,"title":"","content":"Could vampire(ism), just be another Purified-ritual? After all, in both rituals/creation, you have to die first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-14T17:31:08-07:00","id":1553821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1553815#post1553815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could vampire(ism), just be another Purified-ritual? After all, in both rituals/creation, you have to die first.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampirism is the result of a lot of different processes. A Purified ritual gone wrong in just the right way might infect someone with some strain of vampirism, but considering the number of forms of ritually-instilled forms of immortality that kill you if you mess them up and/or if you do them right, being Kindred is pretty clearly not part of the standard set of outcomes for turning your soul into a spirit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-14T19:58:43-07:00","id":1553827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1553821#post1553821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampirism is the result of a lot of different processes. A Purified ritual gone wrong in just the right way might infect someone with some strain of vampirism, but considering the number of forms of ritually-instilled forms of immortality that kill you if you mess them up and/or if you do them right, being Kindred is pretty clearly not part of the standard set of outcomes for turning your soul into a spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vamprism is exactly like the Purifed's, but it is a process of immortality; perhaps it started as a ritual to trap, &quot;The Beast&quot;, in a human-body, but, the Beast isn't in total-control, like a failed spirit-possession.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-14T20:53:48-07:00","id":1553829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1553827#post1553827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vamprism is exactly like the Purifed's,</div> </div> </div> </div>It really isn't. The only thing they have in common is immortality.<br /> <br /> All the methods of becoming Purified require months or years of training and entering the Shadow in addition to dying, and the Beast is sufficiently abstract that a case can legitimately be made for most of the things vampires attribute to it being a defense mechanism against acknowledging their own darker urges.<br /> <br /> Again, a failed Purification ritual might rarely result in a vampire, but vampirism has lots of potential causes that have nothing to do with the Purified.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-26T19:35:05-07:00","id":1554029,"title":"","content":"I was reading the NWoD book last night, about moving wounds to the right, if you have bruised, and you get a lethal; OK, but that's complicated; why not, just upgrade the wounds as they get them. Mark that bruised to a lethal and move on. Will this cause, characters/NPcs to be a bit stronger as they get less wounds; maybe the ST can balance that out?<br /> <br /> Mortals heal way too fast, for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-26T20:41:36-07:00","id":1554030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1554029#post1554029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was reading the NWoD book last night, about moving wounds to the right, if you have bruised, and you get a lethal; OK, but that's complicated; why not, just upgrade the wounds as they get them. Mark that bruised to a lethal and move on. Will this cause, characters/NPcs to be a bit stronger as they get less wounds; maybe the ST can balance that out?<br /> <br /> Mortals heal way too fast, for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not complicated, just wordy. It's actually pretty intuitive to apply, and makes a lot of sense.<br /> <br /> Removing it would take a lot of the benefit out of dealing more severe damage to someone already with less severe damage, as they would upgrade without moving through Health Boxes, and would weirdly be more beneficial to Mortals, as they would be out of combat with any kind of damage, so filling all boxes is what matters most. It would also affect how fast anyone gets damage penalties, as everyone gets them regardless of the type of damage in their last three boxes.<br /> <br /> Mortals heals faster because this game is centered on them. Mortals in CoD are meant to be relevant characters even in splat games, and valid character choices for any game. Valid for real, not &quot;valid under extremely contrived circumstances because the rules are there to make you miserable, expendable and fragile&quot; like in WoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-26T22:08:26-07:00","id":1554031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1554029#post1554029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was reading the NWoD book last night, about moving wounds to the right, if you have bruised, and you get a lethal; OK, but that's complicated; why not, just upgrade the wounds as they get them. Mark that bruised to a lethal and move on. Will this cause, characters/NPcs to be a bit stronger as they get less wounds; maybe the ST can balance that out?<br /> <br /> Mortals heal way too fast, for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>The practical effect of more severe types of damage is in how long a time the character's Health track is effectively shortened for, so having more severe damage overwrite less severe damage effectively means having less severe damage marked going into a fight with something capable of more severe damage is only a disadvantage if you're low enough to be suffering wound penalties, and that wound penalty does not meaningfully run the immediate risk of getting worse because you have to take enough of the more severe damage to pass the less severe damage.<br /> <br /> That works fine for mild and severe Clarity damage in Changeling 2e because Clarity doesn't recover naturally over time, but more severe Health damage takes more time (or, for the Kindred, more Vitae) to heal such that a character with seven Health boxes and three aggravated wounds functionally has four Health boxes barring magical assistance or a lot of downtime, and if more severe damage doesn't move less severe damage down then that means a character who has been beaten halfway to blacking out in a fistfight is not meaningfully easier to knock out with a solid hit form a baseball bat than a fresh combatant.<br /> <br /> It's very simple:<br /> \u2022 You have the number of marked Health boxes equal to the successes and weapon modifiers on any attacks that have hit you.<br /> \u2022 Damage is always sorted into the Health track in descending order of severity, with bashing damage floating on top of lethal damage and lethal damage floating on top of aggravated damage; the least severe damage type is the first one that heals and the one whose effects kick in first.<br /> \u2022 If marking more new damage brings your total above your maximum number of Health boxes, any excess damage is lost as the effective floor on more severe damage moves up; if you already had as much bashing or lethal damage filled in as your Health track can fit, new damage of the same type upgrades to the next level of severity and moves the amount of marked lethal or aggravated damage up accordingly.<br /> <br /> This means it takes a relatively long time for most people to beat someone to deal with their bare hands if they can't be rendered unconscious and therefore vulnerable to a Killing Blow, and it also means each &quot;layer&quot; of the Health track does not interact with the ones above it unless that damage type is achieved directly (e.g. using scarce and dangerous supernatural powers to deal aggravated damage) or the long way (i.e. the reward for dealing enough bashing damage to roll over into lethal damage even against a foe that can't be knocked unconscious is that even if they heal the bashing damage relatively fast, healing all their bashing damage will still leave them with a lessened capacity to take bashing damage). A character with 7 Health who takes exactly 8 bashing damage every two hours will be dead in eight hours rather than fourteen (assuming no bleeding out), because the second instance of damage is hitting a Health track with 6 open boxes, and the third instance is hitting a Health track with 4 open boxes, and then the fourth instance is upgrading a full track of lethal damage to agg.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-27T03:06:54-07:00","id":1554032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1554029#post1554029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mortals heal way too fast, for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that difficult to change. The damage mechanics are already highly abstract, so the healing times are basically arbitrary. Also worth bearing in mind that these are just mechanics. Like, nothing says just because your health track has fully healed that your character has to have fully healed, it just doesn't have an impact mechanically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-03T19:57:23-07:00","id":1554135,"title":"","content":"whats the name of the 2nd edition innocents boook know it exists and has rules for teens too","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"