ategory/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1554163#post1554163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I've read somewhere that Sekhem is older than the Supernal... how the hell does that work?</div> </div> </div> </div>You read wrong. Metaphysically, Sekhem is the stuff that manifest existence is made of, differentiating into the Pillars and from there into other phenomena like those under the purviews of the Subtle and Gross Arcana. The Supernal defines time, space, and the rest of reality through its function as a symbolic interface between the concrete and the abstract, but for the most part it doesn't proactively interfere with Phenomenal reality without &quot;external&quot; interaction by mages or other Mysteries \u2014 the Supernal has an &quot;age&quot; only insofar as interactions with it take place in relation to beings who inhabit a historical perspective.<br /> <br /> See &quot;Crossover in the Conquered Land&quot; in the Dark Eras Companion (p135-140) for the bulk of crossover discussion not covered in the &quot;Mummies and Awakened Magic&quot; sidebar in the 2e corebook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-26T19:53:09-08:00","id":1557028,"title":"","content":"How does choosing flaws work in regards to XP gained? I'm creating an NPC that's dwarf; how much extra XP I should give him for having that flaw, if any?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-26T21:20:03-08:00","id":1557035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1557028#post1557028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does choosing flaws work in regards to XP gained? I'm creating an NPC that's dwarf; how much extra XP I should give him for having that flaw, if any?</div> </div> </div> </div>1e ChroD has Flaws work like Persistent Conditions do in 2e: you get an experience point once per session if it caused problems for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"user