src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-25T08:26:40-08:00","id":1557898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1557478#post1557478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've tried looking through them with word searches, don't see anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still haven't found general guidelines, but the list of vehicles in Deviant's Clades Companion includes Availability for twenty different types of vehicle, which should be a decent sample size and which I'm noting here in case anyone else needs to know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-15T22:39:09-07:00","id":1560010,"title":"","content":"This one might not be as simple as it sounds, since it concerns a potential discrepancy between gamelines: What is the requirement for a character to be able to spend Willpower on a Clash of Wills roll, vis-a-vis physical presence?<br /> <br /> The majority of gamelines (Vampire, Werewolf, Promethean, Hunter, Demon, Beast) use some variation on the earliest iteration of the text, which states that characters can spend Willpower to bolster the contested roll involved in a Clash of Wills, but only if they are physically present and aware that powers are Clashing (typically followed by the note on how increasing duration of an effect adds an increasing number of dice to its roll to Clash with other powers).<br /> <br /> Mage doesn't mention physical presence in its iteration of the mechanic at all but does specify that the Awakened always count as being aware of when their spells are Clashing, which is pretty clearly meant to interface with the requirement (not directly stated here) that a character be aware of Clashing powers to spend Willpower; it also includes the scaling bonus dice from effect duration, as makes sense for the breadth of adjustments that can be made to the parameters of spells. By the opposite token, Deviant doesn't mention spending Willpower or scaling bonus Clash dice from effect duration at all, because the design principles for Variations specifically preclude long-term effects, though the logical endpoint of the scale is included in the form of &quot;powers that are permanently active add +5 dice to their Clash rolls.&quot;<br /> <br /> Geist uses a notably different format from the most common one to more or less the same result, with the biggest adjustments being the changing of the duration-based bonus dice from a paragraph to a table and the ambiguity of characters only being able to spend Willpower &quot;if they're both physically present and aware that two abilities are in conflict,&quot; which seems logically intended as &quot;both of these criteria need to be true for a character to spend Willpower on a Clash roll&quot; but has room to also be read as a different statement, expressed anon.<br /> <br /> Changeling and Mummy both use slight variations on the formatting found in Geist, including the duration bonus table; notable differences include Changeling and Mummy's versions specifying that having awareness of clashing powers to allow Willpower spending may require magic, and that a character can only spend Willpower on the Clash roll if he and his opponent are physically present.<br /> <br /> That last one is\u2026 a very different thing from a stipulation that clearly exists to incentivize characters who expect magical effects they maintain separately from themselves (e.g. Oubliette, the Boneyard, Facets of the Gift of Warding, etc) to need the ludonarrative bolstering of their being around and actively trying to make sure they remain functional. Deviant's corebook Variations are pretty much all definitionally things the character is physically present to use, and Mage is working with expensive component Traits on the Clash pools and potentially messing with time and space in the execution (to say nothing of how it's a gameline that doesn't use Beats to incentivize characters to get severely wounded), but it's not clear why Changeling and Mummy would only allow Clash rolls to be boosted by Willpower in cases where the opposition has the same opportunity.<br /> <br /> Is this a situation where the Geist iteration of the text pre-dates the Changeling and Mummy versions in dev time and was misinterpreted, or is Willpower chicken an intended stipulation of the Clash rules?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-16T02:58:10-07:00","id":1560020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1560010#post1560010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This one might not be as simple as it sounds, since it concerns a potential discrepancy between gamelines: What is the requirement for a character to be able to spend Willpower on a Clash of Wills roll, vis-a-vis physical presence?<br /> <br /> The majority of gamelines (Vampire, Werewolf, Promethean, Hunter, Demon, Beast) use some variation on the earliest iteration of the text, which states that characters can spend Willpower to bolster the contested roll involved in a Clash of Wills, but only if they are physically present and aware that powers are Clashing (typically followed by the note on how increasing duration of an effect adds an increasing number of dice to its roll to Clash with other powers).<br /> <br /> Mage doesn't mention physical presence in its iteration of the mechanic at all but does specify that the Awakened always count as being aware of when their spells are Clashing, which is pretty clearly meant to interface with the requirement (not directly stated here) that a character be aware of Clashing powers to spend Willpower; it also includes the scaling bonus dice from effect duration, as makes sense for the breadth of adjustments that can be made to the parameters of spells. By the opposite token, Deviant doesn't mention spending Willpower or scaling bonus Clash dice from effect duration at all, because the design principles for Variations specifically preclude long-term effects, though the logical endpoint of the scale is included in the form of &quot;powers that are permanently active add +5 dice to their Clash rolls.&quot;<br /> <br /> Geist uses a notably different format from the most common one to more or less the same result, with the biggest adjustments being the changing of the duration-based bonus dice from a paragraph to a table and the ambiguity of characters only being able to spend Willpower &quot;if they're both physically present and aware that two abilities are in conflict,&quot; which seems logically intended as &quot;both of these criteria need to be true for a character to spend Willpower on a Clash roll&quot; but has room to also be read as a different statement, expressed anon.<br /> <br /> Changeling and Mummy both use slight variations on the formatting found in Geist, including the duration bonus table; notable differences include Changeling and Mummy's versions specifying that having awareness of clashing powers to allow Willpower spending may require magic, and that a character can only spend Willpower on the Clash roll if he and his opponent are physically present.<br /> <br /> That last one is\u2026 a very different thing from a stipulation that clearly exists to incentivize characters who expect magical effects they maintain separately from themselves (e.g. Oubliette, the Boneyard, Facets of the Gift of Warding, etc) to need the ludonarrative bolstering of their being around and actively trying to make sure they remain functional. Deviant's corebook Variations are pretty much all definitionally things the character is physically present to use, and Mage is working with expensive component Traits on the Clash pools and potentially messing with time and space in the execution (to say nothing of how it's a gameline that doesn't use Beats to incentivize characters to get severely wounded), but it's not clear why Changeling and Mummy would only allow Clash rolls to be boosted by Willpower in cases where the opposition has the same opportunity.<br /> <br /> Is this a situation where the Geist iteration of the text pre-dates the Changeling and Mummy versions in dev time and was misinterpreted, or is Willpower chicken an intended stipulation of the Clash rules?</div> </div> </div> </div>It s hard to say and as you know the rules of the various splats are a cut n paste hell.<br /> For the narrator sanity i would suggest to take a unifued approach: if the character is somewhat in control (can turn off or modify) of the power or while activating it, then the expenditure is possible. <br /> Considering this premise, about knowing if your power is being clashed, i think that powers contrasting the effective activation (ephemeral shield vs numina) allows for both character the expenditure.<br /> Powers that try to fool magical perceptions (obfuscate vs auspex) are somewhat different as their function is to elude notice.<br /> I would homebrew that the &quot;piercer&quot; cannot notice the clash, but could still spend willpower on an &quot;hypotethical&quot; one if so desired (&quot;i don t know if i clash while activating auspex but i spend the willpower if i will).<br /> <br /> That said, i consider the rule of 1 Willpower per turn so in many cases the player are simply not allowed to use Willpower in clashes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-18T21:56:45-07:00","id":1560083,"title":"","content":"Aa long as they're not in frenzy can someone with 6+ strength spank a child or slap someone in the face witthout breaking- bones","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-18T22:28:01-07:00","id":1560084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1560083#post1560083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aa long as they're not in frenzy can someone with 6+ strength spank a child or slap someone in the face witthout breaking- bones</div> </div> </div> </div>You may reasonably assume, in the absence of specific effects to the contrary, that characters have enough presence of mind and control of their body to not cause wildly excessive damage when interacting with their surroundings in a controlled fashion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-31T03:01:17-07:00","id":1560281,"title":"","content":"how much should the diff be increased for lokpicking in a turn","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-31T06:38:27-07:00","id":1560286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1560281#post1560281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how much should the diff be increased for lokpicking in a turn</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the circumstances. Time alone isn't likely to offer any sort of penalty on the first roll, but subsequent attempts after failure, as well as background noise, magical or chemical inhibition, or a disorganized lockpicking kit all might reduce the number of dice you roll for your character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-13T18:19:28-07:00","id":1560606,"title":"","content":"It's gonna eventually happen; in the book, Immortals, the Purified will eventually lose their body; can they pick up the Body-Thief template and become, truly immortal?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-13T23:29:54-07:00","id":1560609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1560606#post1560606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's gonna eventually happen; in the book, Immortals, the Purified will eventually lose their body; can they pick up the Body-Thief template and become, truly immortal?</div> </div> </div> </div>The versions of the Purified in both Immortals and Book of Lasting Death have the ability to reconstitute their body by spending Essence, with different stipulations on ritually preparing a chamber that allows them to restore their bodies in that location instead of where their physical remains are.<br /> <br /> There's a sidebar in their chapter of Immortals that specifies that Purified can't gain or retain any of the typical templates, and the Body Thieves chapter of the same book both explicitly states that the body thief template is mutually exclusive with most other templates except with Storyteller discretion and has a sidebar on a body-swap-style body theft ritual that specifically doesn't work on any other types of immortal except the ones in that book that involve a recurring process (i.e. blood bathers, patchwork people, and other body thieves).<br /> <br /> Mummy 2e doesn't even have to go to these lengths, as the Endless Template it uses for all its immortals has deciding the method of immortality the character uses as a set step distinct from any other rituals or resources they know or have.<br /> <br /> The Deathless are the only truly immortal worldly beings in Mummy 2e, with the Endless all dealing with some level of cost-of-doing-business problems that drive them into conflict with the Arisen since relics and Sekhem are attractive prospects to tangle for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-19T16:24:51-07:00","id":1561946,"title":"","content":"ideas of how to justify raising Attributes or abilities?<br /> <br /> A gangrel in the ordo dracul Would definitely benefit from Medicine when using Surgical heart removal As would any promethean but an unfleshed creating offspring<br /> <br /> Neither is likely to be able to go to medical school ditto with an invictus needing to learn either Law or political science","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 07-19-2026, 07:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-19T16:34:44-07:00","id":1561947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1561946#post1561946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ideas of how to justify raising Attributes or abilities?<br /> <br /> A gangrel in the ordo dracul Would definitely benefit from Medicine when using Surgical heart removal As would any promethean but an unfleshed creating offspring</div> </div> </div> </div>Exercise, study, and training, same as the narrative justification for having ratings at character creation. Supernatural methods of incrementally or abruptly increasing your talent or competence where appropriate, like drinking the blood of doctors or seeking out replacement limbs from more muscular people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-28T05:09:26-07:00","id":1562254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1560010#post1560010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this a situation where the Geist iteration of the text pre-dates the Changeling and Mummy versions in dev time and was misinterpreted, or is Willpower chicken an intended stipulation of the Clash rules?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's misinterpretation.<br /> <br /> You can rule that Changelings need Conflict\u2122 to Clash, but I don't find it compelling and don't know how you could explain mummies here.<br /> <br /> Another possibility is that this is an intended direction for future rulings, all splats being now required to have the opponent present. It isn't RAW, but may be RAI. Picture the expenditure less as the powers directly Clashing and more the characters defying each other's wills during the Clash, making things personal.<br /> <br /> But tbh I always found this ruling on Willpower spending weird. How does a character infuses their will on an extant effect already in place? I don't think this is impossible to explain, but I do think it should have been explained. A clearer understanding of the metaphysics involved would help a lot to judge this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-08T08:24:01-07:00","id":1564611,"title":"","content":"For Mystery Cult Initiation, <b>what happens when the merit gives you a benefit you already have or do not qualify for?</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Let me use this sample Cult:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 500px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Rating</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Rank</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Benefit</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">\u2022</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">First</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Obtain a <b>Dogs </b>specialty in <b>Animal Ken</b>.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">\u2022\u2022</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Second</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Receive the merit <b>Area of Expertise (Dogs)</b>.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">\u2022\u2022\u2022</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Third</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Gain a dot of <b>Animal Ken</b>.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Fourth</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Gain the <b>Tell (Phantom Pack)</b> merit.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Fifth</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Gain the <b>Pack Bond 3</b> merit.</td> </tr> </table></div> <br /> And our friend Jack, an ordinary human, with no dots of Animal Ken, gets the first rank of the Initiation.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Does he get the specialty but can not use? Use only for Attribute + Specialty rolls? Does it get to be &quot;on hold&quot; until he gets a dot of Animal Ken? Substitue for something else?</li> <li>He gets the second rank, and does not fulfil the Resolve prerequisite, what happens with this merit?</li> <li>After months of effort he rises Animal Ken to 5 dots, and then he gets the third rank in the Mystery Cult... What happens with this extra dot of Animal Ken? With the previous merit and skill specialty?</li> <li>He rises to the fourth level, he becomes automatically a Wolf-Blooded? Or does he get a replacement merit if he was not Wolf-Blooded?</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 10-08-2026, 12:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-08T12:21:19-07:00","id":1564614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1564611#post1564611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does he get the specialty but can not use? Use only for Attribute + Specialty rolls? Does it get to be &quot;on hold&quot; until he gets a dot of Animal Ken? Substitue for something else?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe it says so you need a dot to have a specialty.<br /> <br /> The other questions are answered by the Mystery Cult Initiation merit in the Mage 2e core on page 106:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When this Merit would grant a character a Merit she does not qualify for (such as Awakened-only Merits or Sleepwalker-only ones), she gains the value of the reward in Merit dots instead. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-08T12:31:37-07:00","id":1564615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1564614#post1564614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't believe it says so you need a dot to have a specialty.</div> </div> </div> </div>Deviant specifies that you can't take a Specialty in a Skill with zero dots, Skill Specialties are refinements of existing Skills (Interdisciplinary Specialty even frames the prerequisite as having a certain Skill rating <i>with a Specialty</i>), and the specific nature of unSkilled penalties are such that it would be very weird to, as an example, be able to do first aid at no effective penalty beyond having no Medicine dice because you have three different Medicine Specialties, only one of which can simply be &quot;First Aid.&quot; The first dot of a Skill is needed to be able to start going into the more Experience-efficient specialization of taking Specialties and the Area of Expertise Merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-08T18:52:05-07:00","id":1564622,"title":"","content":"What would, say, Catholic-Priests be in Second Sight? Say a priest had similar powers to one of the merits in the book, which template would they be and which powers would they have? Doesn't have to be Catholic, just Christian-Priests, in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-08T20:19:43-07:00","id":1564628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1564611#post1564611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Mystery Cult Initiation, <b>what happens when the merit gives you a benefit you already have or do not qualify for?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>You get free dots. For both cases.<br /> <br /> As ST I'd consider in a case by case basis the option of giving the Merit even without the requisites if it makes sense in context, but you otherwise just get the dots.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1564615#post1564615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Deviant specifies that you can't take a Specialty in a Skill with zero dots, Skill Specialties are refinements of existing Skills (Interdisciplinary Specialty even frames the prerequisite as having a certain Skill rating <i>with a Specialty</i>), and the specific nature of unSkilled penalties are such that it would be very weird to, as an example, be able to do first aid at no effective penalty beyond having no Medicine dice because you have three different Medicine Specialties, only one of which can simply be &quot;First Aid.&quot; The first dot of a Skill is needed to be able to start going into the more Experience-efficient specialization of taking Specialties and the Area of Expertise Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but that's Deviant and the interpretation is not necessarily as sound as it seems.<br /> <br /> Plenty of people are capable in particular areas and even very skilled at them while being quite ignorant on a lot of related stuff. I've seen all kinds of professionals that even in their overall profession their understanding outside their specializations where below average for the common population.<br /> <br /> So I'd personally allow it no prob. It's weird, but people are weird.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1564622#post1564622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would, say, Catholic-Priests be in Second Sight? Say a priest had similar powers to one of the merits in the book, which template would they be and which powers would they have? Doesn't have to be Catholic, just Christian-Priests, in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>Potentially anything because that's not a clean map of profession/belief to magical practice. And most wouldn't be anything.<br /> <br /> Second Sight templates are pretty individual things. They depend on how that particular person sees and works within that practice, which can vary wildly.<br /> <br /> It's suffice to say: contrary to popular belief most occult grimoires and magical practices of the European Middle Ages were from devout Catholics, a lot of them priests. So anything from External Alchemy (studying the nature of YHWH's Creation) to Internal Alchemy (pray and introspect to awaken the potential of the Faith) to any summoning magic (the authority granted by the Lord to call on His servants and bind Demons) and more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-09T12:36:35-07:00","id":1564648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1564628#post1564628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but that's Deviant and the interpretation is not necessarily as sound as it seems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but it's a simple question thread.<br /> <br /> Also, it's in Deviant's version of the core rules, so I think it's pretty clearly a clarification.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So I'd personally allow it no prob. It's weird, but people are weird. </div> </div> </div>Personally, I've let it bypass the penalty as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-10T14:45:00-07:00","id":1564671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1564628#post1564628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> . . .<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Potentially anything because that's not a clean map of profession/belief to magical practice. And most wouldn't be anything.<br /> <br /> Second Sight templates are pretty individual things. They depend on how that particular person sees and works within that practice, which can vary wildly.<br /> <br /> It's suffice to say: contrary to popular belief most occult grimoires and magical practices of the European Middle Ages were from devout Catholics, a lot of them priests. So anything from External Alchemy (studying the nature of YHWH's Creation) to Internal Alchemy (pray and introspect to awaken the potential of the Faith) to any summoning magic (the authority granted by the Lord to call on His servants and bind Demons) and more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sans True Faith, it's difficult to gauge a priest pitted against Sorcerers. It's World of Darkness: I have to give the priest, <i>something</i>, <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-10T23:20:36-07:00","id":1564681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1564671#post1564671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sans True Faith, it's difficult to gauge a priest pitted against Sorcerers. It's World of Darkness: I have to give the priest, <i>something</i>,</div> </div> </div> </div>First, you don't.<br /> <br /> Even in classic WoD most priests didn't had any True Faith. The point of the Society of Leopold was precisely that they systematically searched through contacts all across the Church for such people, so their recruitment pool was obscene.<br /> <br /> Most priests are just normal humans with theological learning, and their inability to cause actual harm to vampires is the actual point.<br /> <br /> Second and more important, though, what CoD did was ditch the whole pop culture trope for the actual traditions within the Christian faith, because what priests actually do is study. They are academics <i>and occultists</i>.<br /> <br /> What an actual exorcist does is closer to what WoD called a Sorcerer with Faith based Paradigm than that True Faith bullshit. CoD just embraces this take.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:24px\"><b>TL; DR:</b></span><br /> <br /> Your Priest IS a sorcerer in rules terms. He has rituals full of prayers and blessed implements, and attributes his powers to YHWH, but you'll just build as any other practitioner of whatever you want to give him.<br /> <br /> It's RAI, not absence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-11T01:20:21-07:00","id":1564684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1564671#post1564671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sans True Faith, it's difficult to gauge a priest pitted against Sorcerers.</div> </div> </div> </div>What kind of sorcerer did you have in mind?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's World of Darkness: I have to give the priest, <i>something</i>, </div> </div> </div>Do you? Like, a priest seems a fairly good choice for a mortal PC. I'd keep in mind also that in a lot of religious horror, the priest or quasi-priest character precisely doesn't have very much to work with. They have their faith and maybe the rite of exorcism, but the point is that those aren't very reliable.<br /> <br /> That said, some religious rites do 'work', though not for the reasons the mortal thinks they do. The exorcism rules in the core directly refer to Catholic exorcism. Giving someone a proper funeral is implied to work as the Ceremony 'Pass On'. Even having your priest bless your house probably does something to the background spiritual resonance.<br /> <br /> Also, there's the nuclear option of the Malleus Maleficarum from Hunter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-13T13:55:58-07:00","id":1564728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501114-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-cod-general-new-thread?p=1564684#post1564684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What kind of sorcerer did you have in mind?</div> </div> </div> </div>Equally: what kind of priest did you have in mind?<br /> There's not really an equivocation in popular fiction between the Average Sorcerer and the Average Priest. The average priest is not typically working miracles. When they do happen, the priest is usually just as surprised as anyone else.<br /> <br /> There are Special Priests in popular fiction, of course. Priests who have special secret training and experience in fringe practices and contact with the supernatural. Vampires and supernatural exorcists. Those you could give reskinned Supernatural Merits or the like. This is also where Hunter: the Vigil's Malleus Maleficarum, with their supernaturally efficacious Endowment rites, go.<br /> <br /> Chronicles of Darkness as a setting generally shies away from unambiguous confirmation of any particular real world religion. Things get called God's Curse or divine intervention, but there's usually that little asterisk that leads to a rider at the bottom: &quot;we have no evidence this is actually doing what they say it's doing, and in fact we have some incomplete historical scraps suggesting it might be something different and weirder. Either way, though, it does produce this supernatural result.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}